{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe","toolName":"codemode","args":{"code":"for(const p of [\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\",\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\",\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"])text({path:p,content:await tools.read({path:p})});text(await tools.find({pattern:\"*thought*\"}));\n"},"partialResult":{"content":[],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9109159999970871},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9104169999991427},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":1.5290420000019367},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.5485420000004524},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","args":"{\"pattern\":\"*thought*\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":11.119833999997354}]}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe","toolName":"codemode","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16969)\nTotal output lines: 14\n\n==> text 1/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\",\"content\":\"# Repair brief for step build-fix (supervisor, 2026-11-15)\\n\\nRead this file first, then `03-build/output/handoff.md` from the first build step. The approved scope is unchanged: `brief.md` (issue #864).\\nCandidate under repair: commit `21277a3` plus `a33c440` on branch `issue-864-tend-thought`. You have at most 80 responses. Do the items in order.\\n\\n## Observed by the supervisor\\n\\n`python3 scripts/full-check.py` ran on `a33c440` with its normal temporary TEST HOME outside the checkout.\\nRust: all groups passed. Node: 39 passed. Lint and Clippy passed. Python: 84 of 86 files passed. Two files failed:\\n\\n1. `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, line 196, at 80×24:\\n   `AssertionError: Missing '↑↓←→ move   enter open   f connections   l link   esc back'`.\\n   The screen showed `arrows move   enter open   t thought   v read   f connect   l link   esc bac`.\\n   The existing key-bar labels were shortened, and the exit label is cut at 80 columns.\\n2. `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, line 146 (`edits_and_conflicts`): `AssertionError: Missing 'F2 find one connection'`. Cause not yet observed.\\n\\nThe first build's 24 Python failures came from TEST roots placed inside the checkout. Do not repeat that layout.\\n\\n## Repair items\\n\\n1. Key bar. Restore the existing garden key-bar text exactly, at every width the existing tests cover. Do not edit existing tests to fit new text.\\n   Yohaku Article 4 requires a legible exit: `esc back` must never be cut. Show the thought keys without shortening or displacing existing labels.\\n   The thought summary line already names `v read` and `t new thought`; when no thought exists, the `t` key still needs one visible, uncut place.\\n2. `tend_correction_terminal.py`. Reproduce the failure, find the observed cause, and fix that cause. Do not weaken the assertion.\\n3. Reversion probe for \\\"a thought is recorded as a confirmed goal\\\". The first builder failed three times with a hand-built `Affirmed`.\\n   Fresh approach: make the mutation call the existing public `shape::command::new_goal` (the `tinkery seed new` path), which already writes a\\n   confirmed goal session with no Think record. Prove the journey's assertion fails under that mutation, then restore the source and rebuild.\\n   `scripts/probe-thoughts.py` must run all three mutations in one command and exit zero only when each mutation is rejected.\\n4. Robustness, small: one malformed or foreign-format thought file must not hide the other thoughts. Show the readable ones and say how many could not be read.\\n   If this needs more than a small change inside `src/tend/thought.rs`, do not build it; report it instead.\\n\\n## Checks you run\\n\\n- Focused: `tests/tend_thought_terminal.py`, `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_terminal.py`,\\n  `tests/tend_connection_terminal.py`, `tests/test_documentation.py`, then `cargo +stable fmt --all -- --check` and Clippy with `-D warnings`.\\n- Full: `python3 scripts/full-check.py` from the checkout root, unchanged. It creates its own temporary TEST HOME in the system temporary directory.\\n  The supervisor permits that temporary write for this command only. Never point TEST roots at the checkout, the operator HOME or application stores.\\n- After the checks pass on committed work, mark each checklist item with `python3 _system/scripts/sdlc.py mark issue-864-tend-thought <id> passed --evidence <text>`.\\n  Mark an item `failed` or leave it unmarked when its evidence is missing. Do not run `verify`; the supervisor runs it.\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\nNo scope beyond #864. No provider calls, no subagents, no changes to the shared goal saver, session formats, Find connections input or the saved correction.\\nProduct-shape choices (key letters, the word \\\"thought\\\") stay as built; list any doubt in the report for the operator.\\nAfter two failed fixes of one defect, add logging and collect observations. After three, stop and report problem, goal and failed attempts.\\nCommit before you end. Write the report at the path in your step contract, result first, with counts for Rust, Node, Python files, journeys and probes.\\n\"}\n==> text 2/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Build handoff\\n\\n## Situation\\n\\nThe implementation is committed. The run is not ready for acceptance.\\nFull checks fail, and the confirmed-goal reversion probe remains incomplete.\\n\\n- Run ID: `d50e7a87-1232-43e5-a29a-0cbf2512c1ab`.\\n- Checkout: `/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/tinkery/issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Code candidate: `21277a33dc5d469c7ee9ad880fd013c8d31bd8ad`.\\n- Branch: `issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Approved input: `runs/issue-864-tend-thought/brief.md`, from issue #864.\\n- Issue body SHA-256: `29f447833355967617805c1fc76789f53c35598279aa8b5a4f7ba921cf6aa3b1`.\\n- This light run has no seed-contract binding in `run.json`.\\n- Step pin: `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium`. I did not change it.\\n- No PR, independent review, operator acceptance or SDLC verification receipt was created.\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nTend now keeps raw thoughts separately from saved goal sessions.\\n\\n- In the repository garden, `t` opens an exact-word editor.\\n- The editor displays the repository before `F2` saves without a model call.\\n- The garden labels saved entries as thoughts. `v` opens the local thought reader.\\n- Identical bytes in one repository produce one entry and an explicit duplicate notice.\\n- `g` opens the selected words in Think, unsent. Existing goal confirmation remains necessary.\\n- Thoughts cannot open Shape. Find connections still reads saved goals only.\\n- Thoughts use private atomic files in the existing Tend link root.\\n- The new format stores only `schema`, `repo` and `words`.\\n- Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes. They have no edit or delete action.\\n\\nThe exact-word editor moved from `src/shape/words.rs` to shared `src/words.rs`.\\nIts six existing tests moved unchanged. No shared goal saver or session format changed.\\nNo storage service, provider endpoint or migration was added.\\n\\nThe architecture diagnostics affected are 1, 3, 6 and 7.\\nThought persistence stays inside Tend. The menu alone connects a thought to Think.\\nShape and Tend share one editor rather than separate copies of its line-ending rules.\\n\\nSkills read in full:\\n\\n- `principle-build-the-lever` led to a repeatable PTY test and `scripts/probe-thoughts.py`.\\n- `unslop` kept the documentation and notices direct about saving, confirmation and failure.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n### Checked acceptance evidence\\n\\n`tests/tend_thought_terminal.py` passed on the committed code candidate.\\nIt runs six top-level journeys across 80×24 and 100×30 terminals, without colour.\\nIt launches 12 terminal processes with temporary TEST roots.\\nSave, restart, duplicate, cancellation and store-refusal actions make no provider requests.\\nConnection and goal-confirmation checks use local executable stubs, not live providers.\\n\\n1. Checked exact received UTF-8 bytes after explicit saving, including CRLF, CR, tabs, Unicode and trailing whitespace.\\n2. Checked restart discovery, thought labels and isolation between two repositories.\\n3. Checked unchanged goal-session files and confirmation records after thought saves. Pressing `s` does not open Shape.\\n4. Checked Find connections succeeds with thoughts present. Its request contains only the two original goal sources.\\n5. Checked duplicate saving leaves one record and displays `Thought already saved. One entry.`\\n6. Checked the existing Think review and typed confirmation save a goal. The first original equals the thought bytes.\\n7. Checked cancellation and an unwritable store at both sizes. A failed save keeps the words in the editor.\\n8. Partially checked. Changed-word and provider-source mutations fail their intended assertions. The confirmed-goal mutation is not proven.\\n\\nEach saved thought file also passed a `0600` permission check.\\nThese checks prove mechanics with synthetic words. They do not establish operator acceptance or real-data usefulness.\\n\\n### Check results\\n\\nThe logs beside this report retain the observed results.\\n\\n- `thought-journeys.log`: the focused journeys passed again after the code commit.\\n- `independent-probes.log`: changed-word and provider-source faults were rejected. Sources and binary were restored, then journeys passed.\\n- `node-check.log`: 39 Node tests passed, zero failed.\\n- `lint-check.log`: formatting and workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied.\\n- `python3 tests/test_documentation.py`: 12 tests passed after the documentation update.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed before the code commit.\\n- `full-check.log`: the required full check failed in the Rust wrapper. It stopped before its Node and Python steps.\\n- Rust wrapper totals: 1119 passed, one failed, across 20 reported test groups. This is not a passing workspace result.\\n- `python-check.log`: the separate full Python runner reported 86 files, with 62 passing and 24 failing.\\n\\nAll temporary roots were placed under `target/tmp/tinkery-TEST-build` to respect the checkout-only write boundary.\\nThat layout conflicts with fixtures that require output outside a repository or expect launch outside Git.\\nThe Rust failure is `tests::a_live_limit_counts_both_calls_of_a_send_and_records_the_run` in `examples/think_eval`.\\nIts error is `Live output stays outside the repository and the operator's Seed Me and Tinkery data.`\\n\\nSeveral Python failures show the enclosing checkout as the launch repository.\\nOther failures include changed garden-key expectations, long-path display, label saving and launch-guard behavior.\\nTheir individual causes are not all established. Do not classify every failure as an environment failure.\\nThe complete failing-file list and terminal output remain in `python-check.log`.\\n\\nAn initial separate Python-runner attempt refused the real HOME before launching its checks.\\nThe retained Python log comes from the later attempt with a checkout-local TEST HOME.\\n\\n### Confirmed-goal probe blocker\\n\\nProblem: the faulty confirmed-goal probe stops before it reaches the intended assertion.\\nGoal: prove the regression fails when saving a thought creates a confirmed goal session.\\n\\nThree attempts failed:\\n\\n1. A hand-written terminal declaration failed with `Invalid terminal confirmation declaration or action.`\\n2. The valid terminal constructor reached saving, but returned `The goal save could not be verified. Inspect the recovery session before retrying.`\\n3. A first-line goal instead of the raw multiline goal returned the same save-verification error.\\n\\nBoth final attempts passed an empty context to `Affirmed`.\\nThe lower-level ledger refusal was not exposed, so its cause remains unknown.\\nI stopped further fixes after the third attempt. `probe-failure.log` retains the final failure.\\n\\n`scripts/probe-thoughts.py` restores the original source files and rebuilds in its finalizer.\\nIts full command still fails at this first mutation.\\nThe two independent mutations passed when run separately, without changing the script.\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\nKeep this candidate blocked from acceptance.\\n\\n1. Inspect the lower-level refusal before another confirmed-goal mutation attempt. Then prove the intended assertion fails.\\n2. Establish baseline failures under the permitted TEST-root layout. Obtain permission before using roots outside this checkout.\\n3. Resolve actual regressions and run the full required checks again on committed work.\\n4. Obtain independent review, then continue with the run's verification and acceptance gates.\\n\\nThe approved brief, checklist and step contract were not edited.\\nThe generated `AGENTS.md` block and stage/step runtime files were already uncommitted at entry and remain untouched.\\nNo live endpoint requests, real audio recording, delegation, toolchain changes or Pi infrastructure edits occurred.\\nEvery terminal process started by the focused journeys was closed. No local server was started.\\n\"}\n==> text 3/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Tend and handoff\\n\\nTend holds saved goals and raw repository thoughts; [Shape](#shape) asks its questions with an explicit\\nmodel and budget.\\n\\n## Receipt\\n\\nExplicit successful saving shows `Saved.`, the exact frozen goal block and\\n`Next: shape it into a seed in Shape.`\\n\\n- `s open in tend` opens this session's detail, not the garden.\\n- Esc returns to the menu, including from standalone Think.\\n\\nNothing launches, opens a browser, pastes into a harness or starts implementation.\\nPaths belong in F1 then `h`, with the [think record](think.md#think-record) below\\nthe session path. If recording fails, the goal stays saved; help and a muted receipt\\nnotice disclose the gap. If only reading context was rejected, the successful receipt says\\n`Reading sequence wasn't saved; F1 then h shows why.` The path and full reason remain in\\ntechnical details and the plain-text exit receipt. Notices wrap without clipping in receipt and detail.\\nThe plain-text exit receipt may include recovery locations. Its next step is read\\nfrom the session at exit, through the shared verifier: a verified confirmed seed\\npoints to Approve, a draft to confirming in Shape, and a goal without a seed to\\nshaping. An unverifiable or unreadable session points to checking in Shape, never\\nclaims readiness; other ended sessions are named as ended.\\n\\n## Tend: garden and detail\\n\\nIn this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\\nthe repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\\ncall and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\\n`v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\\n`g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\\nThink goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\\nThoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\\n\\nThoughts use private atomic files under the captured Tend link root, separate from\\nsessions and goal confirmation records. Filenames bind the exact repository path\\nand exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\\nIdentical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\\nWhitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\\nempty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\\nnever edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\\n\\nInside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\\norigin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\\n`a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\\nall goals show without a toggle. Unknown, missing, older or conflicting records\\nnever guess a repo; those goals remain under all. An empty repo view still offers\\n`a`. If any active goal lacks attributable repo information, say `N goals have no\\nreadable repo record. Press a for all goals.`, not that this repo has no goals.\\nExplicit no-repo records are known non-matches; older records without repo\\ninformation are unknown. Only with no unknown active goals or unreadable sessions\\nmay an empty repo view say `No active goals are recorded for this repo.` With\\nunreadable sessions, say `N saved records couldn't be read; this repo may have\\nactive goals. Press a for all goals.` Ended counts remain visible. Reopening Tend\\nstarts with this repo again; explicit receipt or Shape returns still open the\\nexact saved goal, switching to all if necessary.\\n\\nFiltering reads existing records on discovery's worker, never during painting,\\nand writes nothing. Legacy discovery enumerates the Think record root once and\\nreads each JSON record at most once, rebuilding an in-memory attribution index;\\nrefreshes never reuse an earlier index. It shares history's strict validation and\\nrechecks session identity and goal across the scan. Malformed or unsupported files\\nmake every origin unknown; duplicate paths and matching schema-1 records refuse\\nattribution, never choose a winner. The index keeps paths, identities, exact goals\\nand origins, not turns or checks; the 16 MiB per-file limit remains, with no total\\nindex-size cap. Links, identity checks and readiness still use every readable\\nsession, including other repos and ended goals. Use all to link across repos;\\n`a` does nothing during linking, detail, history, help or pending/failed reads.\\n\\nTend displays the visible goals in one static graph, without paging or node cap.\\nEqual hollow Braille rings mean size is unknown; no sizes or merges are known.\\nNeeds lines join only active, uniquely identified endpoints. Missing, ambiguous or\\nended endpoints draw no line; the selected-line summary still names them. Straight\\nlines leave gaps around unrelated rings, never implied junctions or routed paths.\\nExisting sessions stay read-only; linking writes only Tend's store.\\n\\nEnded sessions are omitted. `N ended not shown` and\\n`Links couldn't be read. F1 then h for details.` share the muted incomplete-read\\nrow, joined by ` · `, even with no active goals, and survive navigation. An\\nunreadable-links refusal replaces, rather than repeats, the note. When an empty\\nview's body reports unreadable sessions, the footer keeps ended and link notes\\nwithout repeating that count. This applies to repo and all-goals views, including\\noutside a repository. An incomplete empty all-goals view says `N saved records\\ncouldn't be read, so nothing can be listed. Esc goes back.`, never `No active goals`.\\nOnly when every session was readable and ended, say `No active goals. N ended not\\nshown. Confirm a goal in think to start one.`, not that no sessions exist.\\n\\nLabels use the first saved-goal line, including unstructured goals. They sit above\\nor below rings, clipped with `…` or omitted rather than overlapping or interleaving.\\nThe selected label gets space first and always appears, prefixed `› `; its label\\nand ring are bold, jade with colour. Other labels are muted and rings use ink;\\nnone is italic.\\n\\nThe selected-line footer shows the first goal line in ink, status and relative time\\nmuted, then needs and readiness, e.g. `needs Local records · ready`.\\nValid offsets determine age and order. Timestamp syntax stays unchanged; invalid\\ndates and pre-epoch values remain `time unknown`.\\nUnresolved ids say `1 need not found` or `N needs not found`; no needs adds nothing.\\nShort summaries retain status and time. If these crowd the headline, show the\\nheadline, readiness and `F1 needs`; scrollable Help retains full titles. Ambiguous source\\nidentity says `readiness unknown` and attributes no needs. Refusals use the blank\\nrow before the key bar.\\n\\n| Input | Action |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Right, Down or `j`; Left, Up or `k` | Select next or previous in discovery's newest-first order, clamped; not graph neighbours. |\\n| Enter | Open detail. |\\n| `+` or `=`; `-` | Zoom in; zoom out. |\\n| `H J K L` | Pan left, down, up or right. |\\n| Left press on a ring or label | Select its exact session path; a second press within 500 ms opens it. |\\n| Drag a ring or label; drag empty space; scroll | Move the goal; pan; zoom. |\\n\\nThe key bar is `↑↓←→ move   enter open   l link   esc back` (fits 80 columns).\\nSelection pans offscreen goals into view without resetting zoom. Help, detail,\\nhistory, reading, empty and unavailable states ignore graph input.\\n\\nGraf uses deterministic identity-ordered slots adapted to the canvas, initially\\nat least 12 columns × 6 rows apart, without a physics thread. Crowded gardens\\nrequire navigation, panning or zooming, not simultaneous labels. Moving, panning\\nand zooming write nothing. Refresh preserves positions and viewport for an unchanged\\ngr…6969 tokens truncated…e intake status without `viewer`, `snapshot` or\\n`snapshot_current`; `tinkery seed checks DIR` prints the strict check records. Both are read-only.\\n\\nShape copies no intake command. [Approve](approve.md) owns the one command that\\ncreates a run in the named checkout and imports the seed, so a seed has one handoff\\nline and no placeholder to replace (#466). Seed ready points there; choosing or\\ncreating an SDLC run stays outside Shape.\\n\\n### The screen\\n\\n- Under `tinkery › shape` and `?`, content begins at the body top, at most 76 columns\\n  wide. The goal headline or draft, then stage, precedes words, notices and `Next:`.\\n  Overflow scrolls while the words box and cursor, or running status, stay visible,\\n  occupying at most half the body. Cursor following survives long or wrapped\\n  words and resize. Readings (seed plus review or feedback, and So far) must stay under 60,000 bytes; otherwise Shape refuses without confirming or changing anything.\\n  An empty reading viewport cannot mark a draft read.\\n  Only overflow offers `pgup/dn read` while editing or `↑↓ scroll`\\n  otherwise; overflowing questions shorten the save key to `F2 save + look`.\\n  Seed `Nothing found` stays beside words. Crowded bars reduce gaps to two spaces,\\n  never cut Esc.\\n- **So far** (from F1) is a full help-like page without a key bar: the entire confirmed\\n  goal unchanged, then settled `label: answer` decisions in ledger order. Only\\n  `user` authority shows `(you)`; others show their authority, e.g. `(delegated)`.\\n  Open questions follow in ledger order; held questions say `waits for:` with the earlier\\n  answer labels they need. All current-question findings follow, unchanged and in recorded order. Esc\\n  closes it; ↑↓ scrolls. The fixed last row says `↑↓ scroll · esc close`.\\n  It accepts no words, appears after a read, never during a step; F1 lists it.\\n- Say the next step once: omit `Next:` when the key bar names the stage action;\\n  other states and failure notices keep exactly one.\\n- Words boxes use ratatui-textarea, titled `your answer`, `your words`, `your teach-back`, `your change` or `Folder:`.\\n  Arrows, Home, End, Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right move the cursor; Shift selects.\\n  Ctrl+W or Alt+Backspace deletes a word; Enter inserts a newline except at seed confirmation; Ctrl+U undoes\\n  and Ctrl+R redoes. PgUp and PgDn scroll only the reading, a view less one row. Pasted CR and CRLF\\n  display as breaks; edits preserve untouched raw endings. Under seed words, say seed confirmation is not approval to build.\\n- Running steps keep label, question and typed words muted, with one status\\n  (`Saving your answer.`, then `Answer saved. Looking in NAME for the next question.`),\\n  elapsed seconds and `esc stop`. F1 says a step is running.\\n- Shape opens **Tink Contract rN** with proposed pass/fail checks. Each card shows its\\n  verification method, expected result and any proposed failure case from the review of\\n  those exact draft bytes. The remaining draft and supporting evidence follow.\\n  This display order changes neither `seed-contract.md` nor `tinkery seed` commands.\\n\\n### Answering and confirming\\n\\nConfigured drafting enables these actions; see [Model setup](menu.md#model-setup).\\nShape uses Think's\\n[one key map](think.md#help): F2 runs the action in the key bar, F1 numbers the rest.\\n\\n| Stage | Words | Key/action |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Flagged node | `your reason` | `F2 keep with reason`: keep the answer unchanged and revalidate, no model call |\\n| Flagged operator-answered decision | `replacement answer` after F1 **Revise** | `F2 save revision and look`: replace it, reopen settled dependents, then look |\\n| Current question | `your answer` | `F2 save + look`: save then one step |\\n| Current question | Reason, then revisit condition after F1 **Defer** | `F2 next field`, then `F2 save deferral`: publish deferred, then one step |\\n| Current question | None required | F1 **Delegate**: accept the grounded suggestion, then one step |\\n| No question or seed | None | `F2 look into the next question`: one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your words` | `F2 confirm seed rN`: confirm displayed revision when the words are exactly `confirm` |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your change` after F1 **Revise the draft** | `F2 save + redraft`: save the change as your settled decision, then one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your teach-back` after F1 **Teach back** | `F2 save + compare`: capture words and compare with the draft, one call; Esc restores confirmation words |\\n\\n- **Before confirmation:** the ledger computes the risk summary above confirming, including\\n  reversals detected from earlier settled answers, delegated and assumed choices,\\n  exact acceptance of suggestions, and accepted-versus-chosen-otherwise counts.\\n  Shape displays these words without its own checks or formatter.\\n- **Teach-back:** on a draft, F1's **Teach back** opens optional words about what will and won't be built,\\n  prefilled with any confirmation words already typed, editable in a separate box.\\n  F2 saves them verbatim, then compares in one call behind F2's shared budget,\\n  with no tools or repository access;\\n  opening, typing, help and cancelling do not save or call. Confirmation words remain\\n  untouched. The latest completed comparison for these draft bytes appears as guesses\\n  above the risk summary; mismatches are recorded verbatim and never block confirming.\\n  Failed comparisons retain captured words. Confirming without a completed comparison records\\n  `Skipped teach-back.` verbatim, after ordinary confirmation refusals. These append-only\\n  confirmed-goal receipts are bound to the revision and SHA-256 of draft bytes;\\n  confirmation digests cover them. They retain the existing receipt format and are\\n  interview records, not evidence changes or permission.\\n  F1 offers teach-back only on a draft.\\n- **Revise the draft (#614):** on a draft, F1's **Revise the draft** opens `your change`,\\n  prefilled with the confirmation words unless they are `confirm`, so a correction typed where\\n  `confirm` goes is never lost. F2 saves the words verbatim as a settled `change-to-rN` decision\\n  with the operator's authority, never a confirmation, then takes one drafting step behind F2's\\n  budget gate; the redraft lists the change under Decisions. Empty words or words that leave the\\n  change open are refused, saving nothing. Esc keeps the confirmation words untouched.\\n- **Defer:** F1's **Defer** opens the reason; F2 advances to the revisit condition; Tab switches\\n  between them. The form shows the question's gate: the operator alone decides it can wait.\\n  F2 on the condition saves both fields verbatim as `deferred`, never confirmed or settled.\\n  An answer, revision, revisit or delegated suggestion that is empty or only says the\\n  decision is open (\\\"not decided.\\\", \\\"TBD\\\") is refused, saving nothing and keeping the typed\\n  words, and points here (#594).\\n- **Answer deferred prerequisite:** an active Waiting session may offer one named deferred\\n  blocker in F1, selected by the ledger in its existing order. Its own prerequisites and\\n  predicate must be ready; the goal and flagged sessions never qualify. The form shows the\\n  original question, exact deferral reason and revisit condition. Opening, typing and Esc\\n  save nothing. F2 saves the exact answer with existing authorization, locking and stale-state\\n  checks, without a model call. Existing history preserves the prior deferral unchanged;\\n  dependent questions stay unanswered and follow ordinary ready ordering. No picker or\\n  automatic repair is provided. This keeps dependency selection and transitions in the\\n  ledger (architecture diagnostic 6).\\n- **Delegate:** F1's **Delegate** row is one choice, quoting that row as the authority source, saving the\\n  recorded suggestion unchanged with `delegated` authority and its supporting facts as evidence.\\n  Reply confidence is not appended to the recommendation or answer; the ledger never parses\\n  suggestion text.\\n  Missing facts or suggestion refuses without writing; type an answer instead.\\n- **Revise:** only flagged decisions answered by the operator (including delegated answers)\\n  offer F1 **Revise**. Flagged findings (facts and inferences) and the confirmed goal offer only\\n  keep-with-reason; Revise is not shown. There is no settled-answer picker: So far remains read-only.\\n  F2 saves exact replacement words with user authority; the ledger reopens every settled\\n  dependent with a reason naming the changed answer. Shape asks ready dependents one at a time\\n  before a new model question. Saving a revision uses F2's budget gate and next-step path:\\n  an already-recorded dependent is asked without a model call; otherwise one step investigates\\n  or replaces the older draft.\\n- Esc cancels a form without changing the original answer editor. Ledger refusals keep the\\n  question and both typed fields, show the first reason line and allow correction and retry.\\n  Required fields, delegated evidence, revision eligibility and cascading reopen belong only to\\n  the ledger; Shape adds no parallel rules. F1 lists only the actions allowed now.\\n- F2 saves exact answer bytes with `user` authority. Typing, paste, scrolling and\\n  help write nothing; held action keys never repeat. Letters, capitals and `?` remain words.\\n- The chosen harness runs one explicitly selected model with read-only tools (Pi's `read`,\\n  `grep`, `find`, `ls`; Claude Code's `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob` under `dontAsk`), no commands, in the [shown folder](#grounding-in-the-repository). Input includes\\n  the confirmed goal, attributable Think answers, every `found_so_far` finding and\\n  a model-only ledger view: findings appear only in `found_so_far`, not again as\\n  ledger fact nodes or copied decision evidence. Settled pre-mortem questions and answers stay\\n  once in their ledger decision nodes, not a second answer list. Goal provenance, including Think's\\n  original context, stays unchanged; stored ledgers are never trimmed. Replies require typed `found` entries (see\\n  [grounding](#grounding-in-the-repository)) plus a next question and suggestion, or seed summary, prose sections\\n  and separate typed `review` and final `checks` fields;\\n  anything else is a model error. Either reply may include optional `resolves`, a list of\\n  `{\\\"unknown\\\":\\\"FACT-ID\\\",\\\"resolved_by\\\":\\\"DECISION-ID\\\"}` links to an already-settled answer.\\n  Absence means no links; malformed or invalid links refuse the reply plainly, saving no\\n  findings, question or resolution. An answer saved before that step stays saved.\\n  [The ledger](shape-ledger.md#2-what-shape-writes) owns eligibility, history and reopening.\\n  A question may include optional `prerequisites`, a list\\n  of existing decision IDs, preserved unchanged (absent means `[]`). Facts belong in `supported_by`,\\n  not prerequisites. The ledger alone refuses unknown IDs, cycles, invalid lists and deferred\\n  prerequisites (a deferral is not a settled answer), saving no\\n  findings, question or assumptions from a refused reply. A held question stays open without\\n  becoming current; the ledger selects the next ready decision. Once its prerequisites settle,\\n  the held question is promoted before any model call. No reply can settle, skip or reorder\\n  earlier decisions. `src/shape/prompt.txt` has one rule per line.\\n  The decoder tolerates redundant closing braces only after one complete JSON object;\\n  it never reconstructs missing fields or chooses between multiple objects. Invalid\\n  JSON, a missing question and an unsupported reply kind have specific reasons.\\n  The step finds the blast radius and the ways to meet the goal before choosing to ask or draft.\\n- The launch allowance (saved calls or `--shape-budget CALLS`) defaults to zero; each step counts one before the model starts.\\n  With a current question and one run remaining, show `Drafting runs left this launch: 1 of M.`\\n  beside the answer editor before F2 spends it, using Think's shared budget wording.\\n  Budget policy stays behind Agent; Shape owns presentation (architecture diagnostics 3 and 6).\\n  Exhaustion refuses answer, defer, delegate, revision and teach-back before saving anything and explains how to allow calls.\\n- Tinkery, never the model, publishes answers and questions with the displayed version\\n  or the version at step start. Stale versions refuse, retain\\n  typed words and trigger a fresh read, never overwrite.\\n- Tinkery's bundled copy of the [seed contract source](https://github.com/jon-devlapaz/seed-me/blob/c9d766760dbeac0c05c92108165f9e968bec0a66/skills/seed-me/references/seed-contract.md)\\n  defines the artifact. Tinkery's ledger owns its canonical Full heading sequence;\\n  the reply fields and writer derive from that one layout. The model supplies\\n  `confirming` as an object: `You are confirming` contains exactly five non-empty\\n  summary lines, and each model-written prose section has its own string field named\\n  for the section, without heading syntax. Field order is immaterial. The summary\\n  covers goal, what gets built, what does not, the proposed first slice, and unknowns.\\n  Counts and reversal indicators belong to the ledger-computed confirmation summary.\\n  Drafting instructions retain names supplied\\n  in the confirmed goal or Think answers, including in the summary and knowledge\\n  map; a supplied tool name does not settle its executable path or invocation.\\n  Missing, blank, non-string or foreign fields\\n  refuse; prose cannot inject headings, fences, metadata or confirmation lines.\\n  Refusals name the rule and field, plus the offending line for structural text.\\n  A historical Markdown reply beginning `## You are confirming` is refused naming\\n  `confirming`, never with a generic format error.\\n  Shape attaches the bundled reference's section content guidance and check schema,\\n  not its instructions to write or paste artifact headings. The prompt defers to the\\n  generated field instructions, so there is no competing model-written layout.\\n  Tinkery writes every heading, `status: draft`, the goal-headline title,\\n  `revision: rN` one past the previous draft, and a separate `date:` line with the\\n  operator's local date (receipts stay UTC). An older writer can still increment the\\n  revision after rollback. Never replace a confirmed seed or draft with an open decision.\\n  Acceptance criteria, Decisions, Assumed and Evidence and uncertainty come only from\\n  recorded checks, decisions, assumptions and findings, in their canonical positions.\\n  Host-owned headings use LF; prose keeps its line endings. Ledger-owned blocks remain\\n  verbatim, with no extra wrappers. The exact generated title and origin-decision\\n  line treat goal comment markers as literal data during seed verification, only\\n  outside an existing comment. Their text and the confirmed goal remain unchanged;\\n  general heading and prose validation still refuse injected structure.\\n  Findings and question transport are unchanged.\\n- **Completion review runs within drafting**, with no extra call. Before producing a seed,\\n  the step compares settled decisions for contradictions and separates choices (`decided`)\\n  from observed completed work (`done`). Each model check carries its own non-empty\\n  `failure_case` string, including provisional and judge checks. The decoder removes this\\n  model-only field before canonical check validation and pairs it with that check's exact\\n  final statement; the model need not count a second list or copy statements (#469).\\n  A new blocker returns as a question, not a seed. The typed `review` object requires\\n  `contradictions`, `decided` and `done`. Older replies with ordered `review.failure_cases`\\n  strings still work strictly; mixed formats, missing cases and malformed cases refuse.\\n  Tinkery never duplicates, drops or invents cases to make coverage fit. Recorded clinic\\n  count mismatches and statement/case-object replies remain refusals.\\n  Saved check and review formats are unchanged. The ledger's `CompletionReview::validate`\\n\\n[Showing lines 1-716 of 1023 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=717 to continue.]\"}\n==> text 4/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Prove thought protections by introducing three faults, then restore sources and binary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT/'tests'))\\nimport test_launch\\n\\nTHOUGHT = ROOT/'src/tend/thought.rs'\\nCONNECTION = ROOT/'src/tend/connection.rs'\\nFAULTS = [\\n    ('confirmed-goal', THOUGHT, '        let path = self.file(words)?;', '''        crate::seed_me::Config::new(Some(root.parent().unwrap().join(\\\"sessions\\\"))).confirm_as(\\n            crate::seed_me::Affirmed {\\n                goal: words.lines().next().unwrap().trim().into(), outcome: String::new(), options: vec![], originals: vec![],\\n                context: String::new(), source: \\\"TEST faulty thought confirmation\\\".into(),\\n            },\\n            &crate::think_record::GoalConfirmation::terminal(Some(\\\"agent\\\"))?,\\n        )?;\\n        let path = self.file(words)?;''', 'A thought changed goal sessions'),\\n    ('changed-words', THOUGHT, '            words: words.into(),',\\n     '            words: words.trim().into(),', 'Saved words differ from typed words'),\\n    ('provider-source', CONNECTION, '        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));', '''        for entry in fs::read_dir(&self.store).map_err(|e| e.to_string())? {\\n            let path = entry.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.path();\\n            if path.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().starts_with(\\\"thought-\\\") {\\n                let thought: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(path).unwrap()).unwrap();\\n                if thought[\\\"repo\\\"] == serde_json::json!(self.repo) {\\n                    sources.push(Source { id: \\\"TEST-thought\\\".into(),\\n                        goal: thought[\\\"words\\\"].as_str().unwrap().into(), repo: self.repo.clone(),\\n                        status: \\\"active\\\".into() });\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));''', 'A thought reached the provider request'),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    env = test_launch.environment()\\n    output = ROOT/'target/thought-probes'\\n    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    originals = {p: p.read_text() for p in [THOUGHT, CONNECTION]}\\n\\n    def build():\\n        test_launch.run(['cargo', '+stable', 'build', '--locked', '--quiet'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n    try:\\n        for name, path, old, new, expected in FAULTS:\\n            source = originals[path]\\n            if source.count(old) != 1:\\n                raise SystemExit(f'{name}: mutation no longer matches exactly once')\\n            path.write_text(source.replace(old, new))\\n            try:\\n                build()\\n                result = test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env,\\n                                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)\\n                log = result.stdout + result.stderr\\n                (output/f'{name}.log').write_text(log)\\n                if result.returncode == 0 or expected not in log:\\n                    raise SystemExit(f'{name}: protection did not fail for the expected reason\\\\n{log}')\\n                print(f'{name}: rejected ({expected})', flush=True)\\n            finally:\\n                path.write_text(source)\\n    finally:\\n        for path, source in originals.items():\\n            path.write_text(source)\\n        build()\\n    test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    main()\\n\"}\n==> text 5/5 <==\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/thought-journeys.log\nscripts/probe-thoughts.py\nsrc/tend/thought.rs\ntests/tend_thought_terminal.py\n\n[Full output: /var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt (read with offset/limit)]"}],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9109159999970871},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9104169999991427},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":1.5290420000019367},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.5485420000004524},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","args":"{\"pattern\":\"*thought*\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":11.119833999997354}],"fullOutputPath":"/var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt"}},"isError":false,"durationMs":49}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe","toolName":"codemode","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16969)\nTotal output lines: 14\n\n==> text 1/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\",\"content\":\"# Repair brief for step build-fix (supervisor, 2026-11-15)\\n\\nRead this file first, then `03-build/output/handoff.md` from the first build step. The approved scope is unchanged: `brief.md` (issue #864).\\nCandidate under repair: commit `21277a3` plus `a33c440` on branch `issue-864-tend-thought`. You have at most 80 responses. Do the items in order.\\n\\n## Observed by the supervisor\\n\\n`python3 scripts/full-check.py` ran on `a33c440` with its normal temporary TEST HOME outside the checkout.\\nRust: all groups passed. Node: 39 passed. Lint and Clippy passed. Python: 84 of 86 files passed. Two files failed:\\n\\n1. `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, line 196, at 80×24:\\n   `AssertionError: Missing '↑↓←→ move   enter open   f connections   l link   esc back'`.\\n   The screen showed `arrows move   enter open   t thought   v read   f connect   l link   esc bac`.\\n   The existing key-bar labels were shortened, and the exit label is cut at 80 columns.\\n2. `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, line 146 (`edits_and_conflicts`): `AssertionError: Missing 'F2 find one connection'`. Cause not yet observed.\\n\\nThe first build's 24 Python failures came from TEST roots placed inside the checkout. Do not repeat that layout.\\n\\n## Repair items\\n\\n1. Key bar. Restore the existing garden key-bar text exactly, at every width the existing tests cover. Do not edit existing tests to fit new text.\\n   Yohaku Article 4 requires a legible exit: `esc back` must never be cut. Show the thought keys without shortening or displacing existing labels.\\n   The thought summary line already names `v read` and `t new thought`; when no thought exists, the `t` key still needs one visible, uncut place.\\n2. `tend_correction_terminal.py`. Reproduce the failure, find the observed cause, and fix that cause. Do not weaken the assertion.\\n3. Reversion probe for \\\"a thought is recorded as a confirmed goal\\\". The first builder failed three times with a hand-built `Affirmed`.\\n   Fresh approach: make the mutation call the existing public `shape::command::new_goal` (the `tinkery seed new` path), which already writes a\\n   confirmed goal session with no Think record. Prove the journey's assertion fails under that mutation, then restore the source and rebuild.\\n   `scripts/probe-thoughts.py` must run all three mutations in one command and exit zero only when each mutation is rejected.\\n4. Robustness, small: one malformed or foreign-format thought file must not hide the other thoughts. Show the readable ones and say how many could not be read.\\n   If this needs more than a small change inside `src/tend/thought.rs`, do not build it; report it instead.\\n\\n## Checks you run\\n\\n- Focused: `tests/tend_thought_terminal.py`, `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_terminal.py`,\\n  `tests/tend_connection_terminal.py`, `tests/test_documentation.py`, then `cargo +stable fmt --all -- --check` and Clippy with `-D warnings`.\\n- Full: `python3 scripts/full-check.py` from the checkout root, unchanged. It creates its own temporary TEST HOME in the system temporary directory.\\n  The supervisor permits that temporary write for this command only. Never point TEST roots at the checkout, the operator HOME or application stores.\\n- After the checks pass on committed work, mark each checklist item with `python3 _system/scripts/sdlc.py mark issue-864-tend-thought <id> passed --evidence <text>`.\\n  Mark an item `failed` or leave it unmarked when its evidence is missing. Do not run `verify`; the supervisor runs it.\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\nNo scope beyond #864. No provider calls, no subagents, no changes to the shared goal saver, session formats, Find connections input or the saved correction.\\nProduct-shape choices (key letters, the word \\\"thought\\\") stay as built; list any doubt in the report for the operator.\\nAfter two failed fixes of one defect, add logging and collect observations. After three, stop and report problem, goal and failed attempts.\\nCommit before you end. Write the report at the path in your step contract, result first, with counts for Rust, Node, Python files, journeys and probes.\\n\"}\n==> text 2/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Build handoff\\n\\n## Situation\\n\\nThe implementation is committed. The run is not ready for acceptance.\\nFull checks fail, and the confirmed-goal reversion probe remains incomplete.\\n\\n- Run ID: `d50e7a87-1232-43e5-a29a-0cbf2512c1ab`.\\n- Checkout: `/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/tinkery/issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Code candidate: `21277a33dc5d469c7ee9ad880fd013c8d31bd8ad`.\\n- Branch: `issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Approved input: `runs/issue-864-tend-thought/brief.md`, from issue #864.\\n- Issue body SHA-256: `29f447833355967617805c1fc76789f53c35598279aa8b5a4f7ba921cf6aa3b1`.\\n- This light run has no seed-contract binding in `run.json`.\\n- Step pin: `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium`. I did not change it.\\n- No PR, independent review, operator acceptance or SDLC verification receipt was created.\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nTend now keeps raw thoughts separately from saved goal sessions.\\n\\n- In the repository garden, `t` opens an exact-word editor.\\n- The editor displays the repository before `F2` saves without a model call.\\n- The garden labels saved entries as thoughts. `v` opens the local thought reader.\\n- Identical bytes in one repository produce one entry and an explicit duplicate notice.\\n- `g` opens the selected words in Think, unsent. Existing goal confirmation remains necessary.\\n- Thoughts cannot open Shape. Find connections still reads saved goals only.\\n- Thoughts use private atomic files in the existing Tend link root.\\n- The new format stores only `schema`, `repo` and `words`.\\n- Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes. They have no edit or delete action.\\n\\nThe exact-word editor moved from `src/shape/words.rs` to shared `src/words.rs`.\\nIts six existing tests moved unchanged. No shared goal saver or session format changed.\\nNo storage service, provider endpoint or migration was added.\\n\\nThe architecture diagnostics affected are 1, 3, 6 and 7.\\nThought persistence stays inside Tend. The menu alone connects a thought to Think.\\nShape and Tend share one editor rather than separate copies of its line-ending rules.\\n\\nSkills read in full:\\n\\n- `principle-build-the-lever` led to a repeatable PTY test and `scripts/probe-thoughts.py`.\\n- `unslop` kept the documentation and notices direct about saving, confirmation and failure.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n### Checked acceptance evidence\\n\\n`tests/tend_thought_terminal.py` passed on the committed code candidate.\\nIt runs six top-level journeys across 80×24 and 100×30 terminals, without colour.\\nIt launches 12 terminal processes with temporary TEST roots.\\nSave, restart, duplicate, cancellation and store-refusal actions make no provider requests.\\nConnection and goal-confirmation checks use local executable stubs, not live providers.\\n\\n1. Checked exact received UTF-8 bytes after explicit saving, including CRLF, CR, tabs, Unicode and trailing whitespace.\\n2. Checked restart discovery, thought labels and isolation between two repositories.\\n3. Checked unchanged goal-session files and confirmation records after thought saves. Pressing `s` does not open Shape.\\n4. Checked Find connections succeeds with thoughts present. Its request contains only the two original goal sources.\\n5. Checked duplicate saving leaves one record and displays `Thought already saved. One entry.`\\n6. Checked the existing Think review and typed confirmation save a goal. The first original equals the thought bytes.\\n7. Checked cancellation and an unwritable store at both sizes. A failed save keeps the words in the editor.\\n8. Partially checked. Changed-word and provider-source mutations fail their intended assertions. The confirmed-goal mutation is not proven.\\n\\nEach saved thought file also passed a `0600` permission check.\\nThese checks prove mechanics with synthetic words. They do not establish operator acceptance or real-data usefulness.\\n\\n### Check results\\n\\nThe logs beside this report retain the observed results.\\n\\n- `thought-journeys.log`: the focused journeys passed again after the code commit.\\n- `independent-probes.log`: changed-word and provider-source faults were rejected. Sources and binary were restored, then journeys passed.\\n- `node-check.log`: 39 Node tests passed, zero failed.\\n- `lint-check.log`: formatting and workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied.\\n- `python3 tests/test_documentation.py`: 12 tests passed after the documentation update.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed before the code commit.\\n- `full-check.log`: the required full check failed in the Rust wrapper. It stopped before its Node and Python steps.\\n- Rust wrapper totals: 1119 passed, one failed, across 20 reported test groups. This is not a passing workspace result.\\n- `python-check.log`: the separate full Python runner reported 86 files, with 62 passing and 24 failing.\\n\\nAll temporary roots were placed under `target/tmp/tinkery-TEST-build` to respect the checkout-only write boundary.\\nThat layout conflicts with fixtures that require output outside a repository or expect launch outside Git.\\nThe Rust failure is `tests::a_live_limit_counts_both_calls_of_a_send_and_records_the_run` in `examples/think_eval`.\\nIts error is `Live output stays outside the repository and the operator's Seed Me and Tinkery data.`\\n\\nSeveral Python failures show the enclosing checkout as the launch repository.\\nOther failures include changed garden-key expectations, long-path display, label saving and launch-guard behavior.\\nTheir individual causes are not all established. Do not classify every failure as an environment failure.\\nThe complete failing-file list and terminal output remain in `python-check.log`.\\n\\nAn initial separate Python-runner attempt refused the real HOME before launching its checks.\\nThe retained Python log comes from the later attempt with a checkout-local TEST HOME.\\n\\n### Confirmed-goal probe blocker\\n\\nProblem: the faulty confirmed-goal probe stops before it reaches the intended assertion.\\nGoal: prove the regression fails when saving a thought creates a confirmed goal session.\\n\\nThree attempts failed:\\n\\n1. A hand-written terminal declaration failed with `Invalid terminal confirmation declaration or action.`\\n2. The valid terminal constructor reached saving, but returned `The goal save could not be verified. Inspect the recovery session before retrying.`\\n3. A first-line goal instead of the raw multiline goal returned the same save-verification error.\\n\\nBoth final attempts passed an empty context to `Affirmed`.\\nThe lower-level ledger refusal was not exposed, so its cause remains unknown.\\nI stopped further fixes after the third attempt. `probe-failure.log` retains the final failure.\\n\\n`scripts/probe-thoughts.py` restores the original source files and rebuilds in its finalizer.\\nIts full command still fails at this first mutation.\\nThe two independent mutations passed when run separately, without changing the script.\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\nKeep this candidate blocked from acceptance.\\n\\n1. Inspect the lower-level refusal before another confirmed-goal mutation attempt. Then prove the intended assertion fails.\\n2. Establish baseline failures under the permitted TEST-root layout. Obtain permission before using roots outside this checkout.\\n3. Resolve actual regressions and run the full required checks again on committed work.\\n4. Obtain independent review, then continue with the run's verification and acceptance gates.\\n\\nThe approved brief, checklist and step contract were not edited.\\nThe generated `AGENTS.md` block and stage/step runtime files were already uncommitted at entry and remain untouched.\\nNo live endpoint requests, real audio recording, delegation, toolchain changes or Pi infrastructure edits occurred.\\nEvery terminal process started by the focused journeys was closed. No local server was started.\\n\"}\n==> text 3/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Tend and handoff\\n\\nTend holds saved goals and raw repository thoughts; [Shape](#shape) asks its questions with an explicit\\nmodel and budget.\\n\\n## Receipt\\n\\nExplicit successful saving shows `Saved.`, the exact frozen goal block and\\n`Next: shape it into a seed in Shape.`\\n\\n- `s open in tend` opens this session's detail, not the garden.\\n- Esc returns to the menu, including from standalone Think.\\n\\nNothing launches, opens a browser, pastes into a harness or starts implementation.\\nPaths belong in F1 then `h`, with the [think record](think.md#think-record) below\\nthe session path. If recording fails, the goal stays saved; help and a muted receipt\\nnotice disclose the gap. If only reading context was rejected, the successful receipt says\\n`Reading sequence wasn't saved; F1 then h shows why.` The path and full reason remain in\\ntechnical details and the plain-text exit receipt. Notices wrap without clipping in receipt and detail.\\nThe plain-text exit receipt may include recovery locations. Its next step is read\\nfrom the session at exit, through the shared verifier: a verified confirmed seed\\npoints to Approve, a draft to confirming in Shape, and a goal without a seed to\\nshaping. An unverifiable or unreadable session points to checking in Shape, never\\nclaims readiness; other ended sessions are named as ended.\\n\\n## Tend: garden and detail\\n\\nIn this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\\nthe repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\\ncall and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\\n`v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\\n`g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\\nThink goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\\nThoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\\n\\nThoughts use private atomic files under the captured Tend link root, separate from\\nsessions and goal confirmation records. Filenames bind the exact repository path\\nand exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\\nIdentical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\\nWhitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\\nempty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\\nnever edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\\n\\nInside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\\norigin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\\n`a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\\nall goals show without a toggle. Unknown, missing, older or conflicting records\\nnever guess a repo; those goals remain under all. An empty repo view still offers\\n`a`. If any active goal lacks attributable repo information, say `N goals have no\\nreadable repo record. Press a for all goals.`, not that this repo has no goals.\\nExplicit no-repo records are known non-matches; older records without repo\\ninformation are unknown. Only with no unknown active goals or unreadable sessions\\nmay an empty repo view say `No active goals are recorded for this repo.` With\\nunreadable sessions, say `N saved records couldn't be read; this repo may have\\nactive goals. Press a for all goals.` Ended counts remain visible. Reopening Tend\\nstarts with this repo again; explicit receipt or Shape returns still open the\\nexact saved goal, switching to all if necessary.\\n\\nFiltering reads existing records on discovery's worker, never during painting,\\nand writes nothing. Legacy discovery enumerates the Think record root once and\\nreads each JSON record at most once, rebuilding an in-memory attribution index;\\nrefreshes never reuse an earlier index. It shares history's strict validation and\\nrechecks session identity and goal across the scan. Malformed or unsupported files\\nmake every origin unknown; duplicate paths and matching schema-1 records refuse\\nattribution, never choose a winner. The index keeps paths, identities, exact goals\\nand origins, not turns or checks; the 16 MiB per-file limit remains, with no total\\nindex-size cap. Links, identity checks and readiness still use every readable\\nsession, including other repos and ended goals. Use all to link across repos;\\n`a` does nothing during linking, detail, history, help or pending/failed reads.\\n\\nTend displays the visible goals in one static graph, without paging or node cap.\\nEqual hollow Braille rings mean size is unknown; no sizes or merges are known.\\nNeeds lines join only active, uniquely identified endpoints. Missing, ambiguous or\\nended endpoints draw no line; the selected-line summary still names them. Straight\\nlines leave gaps around unrelated rings, never implied junctions or routed paths.\\nExisting sessions stay read-only; linking writes only Tend's store.\\n\\nEnded sessions are omitted. `N ended not shown` and\\n`Links couldn't be read. F1 then h for details.` share the muted incomplete-read\\nrow, joined by ` · `, even with no active goals, and survive navigation. An\\nunreadable-links refusal replaces, rather than repeats, the note. When an empty\\nview's body reports unreadable sessions, the footer keeps ended and link notes\\nwithout repeating that count. This applies to repo and all-goals views, including\\noutside a repository. An incomplete empty all-goals view says `N saved records\\ncouldn't be read, so nothing can be listed. Esc goes back.`, never `No active goals`.\\nOnly when every session was readable and ended, say `No active goals. N ended not\\nshown. Confirm a goal in think to start one.`, not that no sessions exist.\\n\\nLabels use the first saved-goal line, including unstructured goals. They sit above\\nor below rings, clipped with `…` or omitted rather than overlapping or interleaving.\\nThe selected label gets space first and always appears, prefixed `› `; its label\\nand ring are bold, jade with colour. Other labels are muted and rings use ink;\\nnone is italic.\\n\\nThe selected-line footer shows the first goal line in ink, status and relative time\\nmuted, then needs and readiness, e.g. `needs Local records · ready`.\\nValid offsets determine age and order. Timestamp syntax stays unchanged; invalid\\ndates and pre-epoch values remain `time unknown`.\\nUnresolved ids say `1 need not found` or `N needs not found`; no needs adds nothing.\\nShort summaries retain status and time. If these crowd the headline, show the\\nheadline, readiness and `F1 needs`; scrollable Help retains full titles. Ambiguous source\\nidentity says `readiness unknown` and attributes no needs. Refusals use the blank\\nrow before the key bar.\\n\\n| Input | Action |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Right, Down or `j`; Left, Up or `k` | Select next or previous in discovery's newest-first order, clamped; not graph neighbours. |\\n| Enter | Open detail. |\\n| `+` or `=`; `-` | Zoom in; zoom out. |\\n| `H J K L` | Pan left, down, up or right. |\\n| Left press on a ring or label | Select its exact session path; a second press within 500 ms opens it. |\\n| Drag a ring or label; drag empty space; scroll | Move the goal; pan; zoom. |\\n\\nThe key bar is `↑↓←→ move   enter open   l link   esc back` (fits 80 columns).\\nSelection pans offscreen goals into view without resetting zoom. Help, detail,\\nhistory, reading, empty and unavailable states ignore graph input.\\n\\nGraf uses deterministic identity-ordered slots adapted to the canvas, initially\\nat least 12 columns × 6 rows apart, without a physics thread. Crowded gardens\\nrequire navigation, panning or zooming, not simultaneous labels. Moving, panning\\nand zooming write nothing. Refresh preserves positions and viewport for an unchanged\\ngr…6969 tokens truncated…e intake status without `viewer`, `snapshot` or\\n`snapshot_current`; `tinkery seed checks DIR` prints the strict check records. Both are read-only.\\n\\nShape copies no intake command. [Approve](approve.md) owns the one command that\\ncreates a run in the named checkout and imports the seed, so a seed has one handoff\\nline and no placeholder to replace (#466). Seed ready points there; choosing or\\ncreating an SDLC run stays outside Shape.\\n\\n### The screen\\n\\n- Under `tinkery › shape` and `?`, content begins at the body top, at most 76 columns\\n  wide. The goal headline or draft, then stage, precedes words, notices and `Next:`.\\n  Overflow scrolls while the words box and cursor, or running status, stay visible,\\n  occupying at most half the body. Cursor following survives long or wrapped\\n  words and resize. Readings (seed plus review or feedback, and So far) must stay under 60,000 bytes; otherwise Shape refuses without confirming or changing anything.\\n  An empty reading viewport cannot mark a draft read.\\n  Only overflow offers `pgup/dn read` while editing or `↑↓ scroll`\\n  otherwise; overflowing questions shorten the save key to `F2 save + look`.\\n  Seed `Nothing found` stays beside words. Crowded bars reduce gaps to two spaces,\\n  never cut Esc.\\n- **So far** (from F1) is a full help-like page without a key bar: the entire confirmed\\n  goal unchanged, then settled `label: answer` decisions in ledger order. Only\\n  `user` authority shows `(you)`; others show their authority, e.g. `(delegated)`.\\n  Open questions follow in ledger order; held questions say `waits for:` with the earlier\\n  answer labels they need. All current-question findings follow, unchanged and in recorded order. Esc\\n  closes it; ↑↓ scrolls. The fixed last row says `↑↓ scroll · esc close`.\\n  It accepts no words, appears after a read, never during a step; F1 lists it.\\n- Say the next step once: omit `Next:` when the key bar names the stage action;\\n  other states and failure notices keep exactly one.\\n- Words boxes use ratatui-textarea, titled `your answer`, `your words`, `your teach-back`, `your change` or `Folder:`.\\n  Arrows, Home, End, Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right move the cursor; Shift selects.\\n  Ctrl+W or Alt+Backspace deletes a word; Enter inserts a newline except at seed confirmation; Ctrl+U undoes\\n  and Ctrl+R redoes. PgUp and PgDn scroll only the reading, a view less one row. Pasted CR and CRLF\\n  display as breaks; edits preserve untouched raw endings. Under seed words, say seed confirmation is not approval to build.\\n- Running steps keep label, question and typed words muted, with one status\\n  (`Saving your answer.`, then `Answer saved. Looking in NAME for the next question.`),\\n  elapsed seconds and `esc stop`. F1 says a step is running.\\n- Shape opens **Tink Contract rN** with proposed pass/fail checks. Each card shows its\\n  verification method, expected result and any proposed failure case from the review of\\n  those exact draft bytes. The remaining draft and supporting evidence follow.\\n  This display order changes neither `seed-contract.md` nor `tinkery seed` commands.\\n\\n### Answering and confirming\\n\\nConfigured drafting enables these actions; see [Model setup](menu.md#model-setup).\\nShape uses Think's\\n[one key map](think.md#help): F2 runs the action in the key bar, F1 numbers the rest.\\n\\n| Stage | Words | Key/action |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Flagged node | `your reason` | `F2 keep with reason`: keep the answer unchanged and revalidate, no model call |\\n| Flagged operator-answered decision | `replacement answer` after F1 **Revise** | `F2 save revision and look`: replace it, reopen settled dependents, then look |\\n| Current question | `your answer` | `F2 save + look`: save then one step |\\n| Current question | Reason, then revisit condition after F1 **Defer** | `F2 next field`, then `F2 save deferral`: publish deferred, then one step |\\n| Current question | None required | F1 **Delegate**: accept the grounded suggestion, then one step |\\n| No question or seed | None | `F2 look into the next question`: one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your words` | `F2 confirm seed rN`: confirm displayed revision when the words are exactly `confirm` |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your change` after F1 **Revise the draft** | `F2 save + redraft`: save the change as your settled decision, then one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your teach-back` after F1 **Teach back** | `F2 save + compare`: capture words and compare with the draft, one call; Esc restores confirmation words |\\n\\n- **Before confirmation:** the ledger computes the risk summary above confirming, including\\n  reversals detected from earlier settled answers, delegated and assumed choices,\\n  exact acceptance of suggestions, and accepted-versus-chosen-otherwise counts.\\n  Shape displays these words without its own checks or formatter.\\n- **Teach-back:** on a draft, F1's **Teach back** opens optional words about what will and won't be built,\\n  prefilled with any confirmation words already typed, editable in a separate box.\\n  F2 saves them verbatim, then compares in one call behind F2's shared budget,\\n  with no tools or repository access;\\n  opening, typing, help and cancelling do not save or call. Confirmation words remain\\n  untouched. The latest completed comparison for these draft bytes appears as guesses\\n  above the risk summary; mismatches are recorded verbatim and never block confirming.\\n  Failed comparisons retain captured words. Confirming without a completed comparison records\\n  `Skipped teach-back.` verbatim, after ordinary confirmation refusals. These append-only\\n  confirmed-goal receipts are bound to the revision and SHA-256 of draft bytes;\\n  confirmation digests cover them. They retain the existing receipt format and are\\n  interview records, not evidence changes or permission.\\n  F1 offers teach-back only on a draft.\\n- **Revise the draft (#614):** on a draft, F1's **Revise the draft** opens `your change`,\\n  prefilled with the confirmation words unless they are `confirm`, so a correction typed where\\n  `confirm` goes is never lost. F2 saves the words verbatim as a settled `change-to-rN` decision\\n  with the operator's authority, never a confirmation, then takes one drafting step behind F2's\\n  budget gate; the redraft lists the change under Decisions. Empty words or words that leave the\\n  change open are refused, saving nothing. Esc keeps the confirmation words untouched.\\n- **Defer:** F1's **Defer** opens the reason; F2 advances to the revisit condition; Tab switches\\n  between them. The form shows the question's gate: the operator alone decides it can wait.\\n  F2 on the condition saves both fields verbatim as `deferred`, never confirmed or settled.\\n  An answer, revision, revisit or delegated suggestion that is empty or only says the\\n  decision is open (\\\"not decided.\\\", \\\"TBD\\\") is refused, saving nothing and keeping the typed\\n  words, and points here (#594).\\n- **Answer deferred prerequisite:** an active Waiting session may offer one named deferred\\n  blocker in F1, selected by the ledger in its existing order. Its own prerequisites and\\n  predicate must be ready; the goal and flagged sessions never qualify. The form shows the\\n  original question, exact deferral reason and revisit condition. Opening, typing and Esc\\n  save nothing. F2 saves the exact answer with existing authorization, locking and stale-state\\n  checks, without a model call. Existing history preserves the prior deferral unchanged;\\n  dependent questions stay unanswered and follow ordinary ready ordering. No picker or\\n  automatic repair is provided. This keeps dependency selection and transitions in the\\n  ledger (architecture diagnostic 6).\\n- **Delegate:** F1's **Delegate** row is one choice, quoting that row as the authority source, saving the\\n  recorded suggestion unchanged with `delegated` authority and its supporting facts as evidence.\\n  Reply confidence is not appended to the recommendation or answer; the ledger never parses\\n  suggestion text.\\n  Missing facts or suggestion refuses without writing; type an answer instead.\\n- **Revise:** only flagged decisions answered by the operator (including delegated answers)\\n  offer F1 **Revise**. Flagged findings (facts and inferences) and the confirmed goal offer only\\n  keep-with-reason; Revise is not shown. There is no settled-answer picker: So far remains read-only.\\n  F2 saves exact replacement words with user authority; the ledger reopens every settled\\n  dependent with a reason naming the changed answer. Shape asks ready dependents one at a time\\n  before a new model question. Saving a revision uses F2's budget gate and next-step path:\\n  an already-recorded dependent is asked without a model call; otherwise one step investigates\\n  or replaces the older draft.\\n- Esc cancels a form without changing the original answer editor. Ledger refusals keep the\\n  question and both typed fields, show the first reason line and allow correction and retry.\\n  Required fields, delegated evidence, revision eligibility and cascading reopen belong only to\\n  the ledger; Shape adds no parallel rules. F1 lists only the actions allowed now.\\n- F2 saves exact answer bytes with `user` authority. Typing, paste, scrolling and\\n  help write nothing; held action keys never repeat. Letters, capitals and `?` remain words.\\n- The chosen harness runs one explicitly selected model with read-only tools (Pi's `read`,\\n  `grep`, `find`, `ls`; Claude Code's `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob` under `dontAsk`), no commands, in the [shown folder](#grounding-in-the-repository). Input includes\\n  the confirmed goal, attributable Think answers, every `found_so_far` finding and\\n  a model-only ledger view: findings appear only in `found_so_far`, not again as\\n  ledger fact nodes or copied decision evidence. Settled pre-mortem questions and answers stay\\n  once in their ledger decision nodes, not a second answer list. Goal provenance, including Think's\\n  original context, stays unchanged; stored ledgers are never trimmed. Replies require typed `found` entries (see\\n  [grounding](#grounding-in-the-repository)) plus a next question and suggestion, or seed summary, prose sections\\n  and separate typed `review` and final `checks` fields;\\n  anything else is a model error. Either reply may include optional `resolves`, a list of\\n  `{\\\"unknown\\\":\\\"FACT-ID\\\",\\\"resolved_by\\\":\\\"DECISION-ID\\\"}` links to an already-settled answer.\\n  Absence means no links; malformed or invalid links refuse the reply plainly, saving no\\n  findings, question or resolution. An answer saved before that step stays saved.\\n  [The ledger](shape-ledger.md#2-what-shape-writes) owns eligibility, history and reopening.\\n  A question may include optional `prerequisites`, a list\\n  of existing decision IDs, preserved unchanged (absent means `[]`). Facts belong in `supported_by`,\\n  not prerequisites. The ledger alone refuses unknown IDs, cycles, invalid lists and deferred\\n  prerequisites (a deferral is not a settled answer), saving no\\n  findings, question or assumptions from a refused reply. A held question stays open without\\n  becoming current; the ledger selects the next ready decision. Once its prerequisites settle,\\n  the held question is promoted before any model call. No reply can settle, skip or reorder\\n  earlier decisions. `src/shape/prompt.txt` has one rule per line.\\n  The decoder tolerates redundant closing braces only after one complete JSON object;\\n  it never reconstructs missing fields or chooses between multiple objects. Invalid\\n  JSON, a missing question and an unsupported reply kind have specific reasons.\\n  The step finds the blast radius and the ways to meet the goal before choosing to ask or draft.\\n- The launch allowance (saved calls or `--shape-budget CALLS`) defaults to zero; each step counts one before the model starts.\\n  With a current question and one run remaining, show `Drafting runs left this launch: 1 of M.`\\n  beside the answer editor before F2 spends it, using Think's shared budget wording.\\n  Budget policy stays behind Agent; Shape owns presentation (architecture diagnostics 3 and 6).\\n  Exhaustion refuses answer, defer, delegate, revision and teach-back before saving anything and explains how to allow calls.\\n- Tinkery, never the model, publishes answers and questions with the displayed version\\n  or the version at step start. Stale versions refuse, retain\\n  typed words and trigger a fresh read, never overwrite.\\n- Tinkery's bundled copy of the [seed contract source](https://github.com/jon-devlapaz/seed-me/blob/c9d766760dbeac0c05c92108165f9e968bec0a66/skills/seed-me/references/seed-contract.md)\\n  defines the artifact. Tinkery's ledger owns its canonical Full heading sequence;\\n  the reply fields and writer derive from that one layout. The model supplies\\n  `confirming` as an object: `You are confirming` contains exactly five non-empty\\n  summary lines, and each model-written prose section has its own string field named\\n  for the section, without heading syntax. Field order is immaterial. The summary\\n  covers goal, what gets built, what does not, the proposed first slice, and unknowns.\\n  Counts and reversal indicators belong to the ledger-computed confirmation summary.\\n  Drafting instructions retain names supplied\\n  in the confirmed goal or Think answers, including in the summary and knowledge\\n  map; a supplied tool name does not settle its executable path or invocation.\\n  Missing, blank, non-string or foreign fields\\n  refuse; prose cannot inject headings, fences, metadata or confirmation lines.\\n  Refusals name the rule and field, plus the offending line for structural text.\\n  A historical Markdown reply beginning `## You are confirming` is refused naming\\n  `confirming`, never with a generic format error.\\n  Shape attaches the bundled reference's section content guidance and check schema,\\n  not its instructions to write or paste artifact headings. The prompt defers to the\\n  generated field instructions, so there is no competing model-written layout.\\n  Tinkery writes every heading, `status: draft`, the goal-headline title,\\n  `revision: rN` one past the previous draft, and a separate `date:` line with the\\n  operator's local date (receipts stay UTC). An older writer can still increment the\\n  revision after rollback. Never replace a confirmed seed or draft with an open decision.\\n  Acceptance criteria, Decisions, Assumed and Evidence and uncertainty come only from\\n  recorded checks, decisions, assumptions and findings, in their canonical positions.\\n  Host-owned headings use LF; prose keeps its line endings. Ledger-owned blocks remain\\n  verbatim, with no extra wrappers. The exact generated title and origin-decision\\n  line treat goal comment markers as literal data during seed verification, only\\n  outside an existing comment. Their text and the confirmed goal remain unchanged;\\n  general heading and prose validation still refuse injected structure.\\n  Findings and question transport are unchanged.\\n- **Completion review runs within drafting**, with no extra call. Before producing a seed,\\n  the step compares settled decisions for contradictions and separates choices (`decided`)\\n  from observed completed work (`done`). Each model check carries its own non-empty\\n  `failure_case` string, including provisional and judge checks. The decoder removes this\\n  model-only field before canonical check validation and pairs it with that check's exact\\n  final statement; the model need not count a second list or copy statements (#469).\\n  A new blocker returns as a question, not a seed. The typed `review` object requires\\n  `contradictions`, `decided` and `done`. Older replies with ordered `review.failure_cases`\\n  strings still work strictly; mixed formats, missing cases and malformed cases refuse.\\n  Tinkery never duplicates, drops or invents cases to make coverage fit. Recorded clinic\\n  count mismatches and statement/case-object replies remain refusals.\\n  Saved check and review formats are unchanged. The ledger's `CompletionReview::validate`\\n\\n[Showing lines 1-716 of 1023 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=717 to continue.]\"}\n==> text 4/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Prove thought protections by introducing three faults, then restore sources and binary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT/'tests'))\\nimport test_launch\\n\\nTHOUGHT = ROOT/'src/tend/thought.rs'\\nCONNECTION = ROOT/'src/tend/connection.rs'\\nFAULTS = [\\n    ('confirmed-goal', THOUGHT, '        let path = self.file(words)?;', '''        crate::seed_me::Config::new(Some(root.parent().unwrap().join(\\\"sessions\\\"))).confirm_as(\\n            crate::seed_me::Affirmed {\\n                goal: words.lines().next().unwrap().trim().into(), outcome: String::new(), options: vec![], originals: vec![],\\n                context: String::new(), source: \\\"TEST faulty thought confirmation\\\".into(),\\n            },\\n            &crate::think_record::GoalConfirmation::terminal(Some(\\\"agent\\\"))?,\\n        )?;\\n        let path = self.file(words)?;''', 'A thought changed goal sessions'),\\n    ('changed-words', THOUGHT, '            words: words.into(),',\\n     '            words: words.trim().into(),', 'Saved words differ from typed words'),\\n    ('provider-source', CONNECTION, '        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));', '''        for entry in fs::read_dir(&self.store).map_err(|e| e.to_string())? {\\n            let path = entry.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.path();\\n            if path.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().starts_with(\\\"thought-\\\") {\\n                let thought: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(path).unwrap()).unwrap();\\n                if thought[\\\"repo\\\"] == serde_json::json!(self.repo) {\\n                    sources.push(Source { id: \\\"TEST-thought\\\".into(),\\n                        goal: thought[\\\"words\\\"].as_str().unwrap().into(), repo: self.repo.clone(),\\n                        status: \\\"active\\\".into() });\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));''', 'A thought reached the provider request'),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    env = test_launch.environment()\\n    output = ROOT/'target/thought-probes'\\n    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    originals = {p: p.read_text() for p in [THOUGHT, CONNECTION]}\\n\\n    def build():\\n        test_launch.run(['cargo', '+stable', 'build', '--locked', '--quiet'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n    try:\\n        for name, path, old, new, expected in FAULTS:\\n            source = originals[path]\\n            if source.count(old) != 1:\\n                raise SystemExit(f'{name}: mutation no longer matches exactly once')\\n            path.write_text(source.replace(old, new))\\n            try:\\n                build()\\n                result = test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env,\\n                                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)\\n                log = result.stdout + result.stderr\\n                (output/f'{name}.log').write_text(log)\\n                if result.returncode == 0 or expected not in log:\\n                    raise SystemExit(f'{name}: protection did not fail for the expected reason\\\\n{log}')\\n                print(f'{name}: rejected ({expected})', flush=True)\\n            finally:\\n                path.write_text(source)\\n    finally:\\n        for path, source in originals.items():\\n            path.write_text(source)\\n        build()\\n    test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    main()\\n\"}\n==> text 5/5 <==\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/thought-journeys.log\nscripts/probe-thoughts.py\nsrc/tend/thought.rs\ntests/tend_thought_terminal.py\n\n[Full output: /var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt (read with offset/limit)]"}],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9109159999970871},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9104169999991427},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":1.5290420000019367},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.5485420000004524},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","args":"{\"pattern\":\"*thought*\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":11.119833999997354}],"fullOutputPath":"/var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt"},"isError":false,"durationMs":49,"timestamp":1794733047304,"nestedCalls":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"scripts/probe-thoughts.py"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","status":"ok","arguments":{"pattern":"*thought*"},"durationMs":11}],"complete":true}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe","toolName":"codemode","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16969)\nTotal output lines: 14\n\n==> text 1/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\",\"content\":\"# Repair brief for step build-fix (supervisor, 2026-11-15)\\n\\nRead this file first, then `03-build/output/handoff.md` from the first build step. The approved scope is unchanged: `brief.md` (issue #864).\\nCandidate under repair: commit `21277a3` plus `a33c440` on branch `issue-864-tend-thought`. You have at most 80 responses. Do the items in order.\\n\\n## Observed by the supervisor\\n\\n`python3 scripts/full-check.py` ran on `a33c440` with its normal temporary TEST HOME outside the checkout.\\nRust: all groups passed. Node: 39 passed. Lint and Clippy passed. Python: 84 of 86 files passed. Two files failed:\\n\\n1. `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, line 196, at 80×24:\\n   `AssertionError: Missing '↑↓←→ move   enter open   f connections   l link   esc back'`.\\n   The screen showed `arrows move   enter open   t thought   v read   f connect   l link   esc bac`.\\n   The existing key-bar labels were shortened, and the exit label is cut at 80 columns.\\n2. `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, line 146 (`edits_and_conflicts`): `AssertionError: Missing 'F2 find one connection'`. Cause not yet observed.\\n\\nThe first build's 24 Python failures came from TEST roots placed inside the checkout. Do not repeat that layout.\\n\\n## Repair items\\n\\n1. Key bar. Restore the existing garden key-bar text exactly, at every width the existing tests cover. Do not edit existing tests to fit new text.\\n   Yohaku Article 4 requires a legible exit: `esc back` must never be cut. Show the thought keys without shortening or displacing existing labels.\\n   The thought summary line already names `v read` and `t new thought`; when no thought exists, the `t` key still needs one visible, uncut place.\\n2. `tend_correction_terminal.py`. Reproduce the failure, find the observed cause, and fix that cause. Do not weaken the assertion.\\n3. Reversion probe for \\\"a thought is recorded as a confirmed goal\\\". The first builder failed three times with a hand-built `Affirmed`.\\n   Fresh approach: make the mutation call the existing public `shape::command::new_goal` (the `tinkery seed new` path), which already writes a\\n   confirmed goal session with no Think record. Prove the journey's assertion fails under that mutation, then restore the source and rebuild.\\n   `scripts/probe-thoughts.py` must run all three mutations in one command and exit zero only when each mutation is rejected.\\n4. Robustness, small: one malformed or foreign-format thought file must not hide the other thoughts. Show the readable ones and say how many could not be read.\\n   If this needs more than a small change inside `src/tend/thought.rs`, do not build it; report it instead.\\n\\n## Checks you run\\n\\n- Focused: `tests/tend_thought_terminal.py`, `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_terminal.py`,\\n  `tests/tend_connection_terminal.py`, `tests/test_documentation.py`, then `cargo +stable fmt --all -- --check` and Clippy with `-D warnings`.\\n- Full: `python3 scripts/full-check.py` from the checkout root, unchanged. It creates its own temporary TEST HOME in the system temporary directory.\\n  The supervisor permits that temporary write for this command only. Never point TEST roots at the checkout, the operator HOME or application stores.\\n- After the checks pass on committed work, mark each checklist item with `python3 _system/scripts/sdlc.py mark issue-864-tend-thought <id> passed --evidence <text>`.\\n  Mark an item `failed` or leave it unmarked when its evidence is missing. Do not run `verify`; the supervisor runs it.\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\nNo scope beyond #864. No provider calls, no subagents, no changes to the shared goal saver, session formats, Find connections input or the saved correction.\\nProduct-shape choices (key letters, the word \\\"thought\\\") stay as built; list any doubt in the report for the operator.\\nAfter two failed fixes of one defect, add logging and collect observations. After three, stop and report problem, goal and failed attempts.\\nCommit before you end. Write the report at the path in your step contract, result first, with counts for Rust, Node, Python files, journeys and probes.\\n\"}\n==> text 2/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Build handoff\\n\\n## Situation\\n\\nThe implementation is committed. The run is not ready for acceptance.\\nFull checks fail, and the confirmed-goal reversion probe remains incomplete.\\n\\n- Run ID: `d50e7a87-1232-43e5-a29a-0cbf2512c1ab`.\\n- Checkout: `/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/tinkery/issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Code candidate: `21277a33dc5d469c7ee9ad880fd013c8d31bd8ad`.\\n- Branch: `issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Approved input: `runs/issue-864-tend-thought/brief.md`, from issue #864.\\n- Issue body SHA-256: `29f447833355967617805c1fc76789f53c35598279aa8b5a4f7ba921cf6aa3b1`.\\n- This light run has no seed-contract binding in `run.json`.\\n- Step pin: `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium`. I did not change it.\\n- No PR, independent review, operator acceptance or SDLC verification receipt was created.\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nTend now keeps raw thoughts separately from saved goal sessions.\\n\\n- In the repository garden, `t` opens an exact-word editor.\\n- The editor displays the repository before `F2` saves without a model call.\\n- The garden labels saved entries as thoughts. `v` opens the local thought reader.\\n- Identical bytes in one repository produce one entry and an explicit duplicate notice.\\n- `g` opens the selected words in Think, unsent. Existing goal confirmation remains necessary.\\n- Thoughts cannot open Shape. Find connections still reads saved goals only.\\n- Thoughts use private atomic files in the existing Tend link root.\\n- The new format stores only `schema`, `repo` and `words`.\\n- Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes. They have no edit or delete action.\\n\\nThe exact-word editor moved from `src/shape/words.rs` to shared `src/words.rs`.\\nIts six existing tests moved unchanged. No shared goal saver or session format changed.\\nNo storage service, provider endpoint or migration was added.\\n\\nThe architecture diagnostics affected are 1, 3, 6 and 7.\\nThought persistence stays inside Tend. The menu alone connects a thought to Think.\\nShape and Tend share one editor rather than separate copies of its line-ending rules.\\n\\nSkills read in full:\\n\\n- `principle-build-the-lever` led to a repeatable PTY test and `scripts/probe-thoughts.py`.\\n- `unslop` kept the documentation and notices direct about saving, confirmation and failure.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n### Checked acceptance evidence\\n\\n`tests/tend_thought_terminal.py` passed on the committed code candidate.\\nIt runs six top-level journeys across 80×24 and 100×30 terminals, without colour.\\nIt launches 12 terminal processes with temporary TEST roots.\\nSave, restart, duplicate, cancellation and store-refusal actions make no provider requests.\\nConnection and goal-confirmation checks use local executable stubs, not live providers.\\n\\n1. Checked exact received UTF-8 bytes after explicit saving, including CRLF, CR, tabs, Unicode and trailing whitespace.\\n2. Checked restart discovery, thought labels and isolation between two repositories.\\n3. Checked unchanged goal-session files and confirmation records after thought saves. Pressing `s` does not open Shape.\\n4. Checked Find connections succeeds with thoughts present. Its request contains only the two original goal sources.\\n5. Checked duplicate saving leaves one record and displays `Thought already saved. One entry.`\\n6. Checked the existing Think review and typed confirmation save a goal. The first original equals the thought bytes.\\n7. Checked cancellation and an unwritable store at both sizes. A failed save keeps the words in the editor.\\n8. Partially checked. Changed-word and provider-source mutations fail their intended assertions. The confirmed-goal mutation is not proven.\\n\\nEach saved thought file also passed a `0600` permission check.\\nThese checks prove mechanics with synthetic words. They do not establish operator acceptance or real-data usefulness.\\n\\n### Check results\\n\\nThe logs beside this report retain the observed results.\\n\\n- `thought-journeys.log`: the focused journeys passed again after the code commit.\\n- `independent-probes.log`: changed-word and provider-source faults were rejected. Sources and binary were restored, then journeys passed.\\n- `node-check.log`: 39 Node tests passed, zero failed.\\n- `lint-check.log`: formatting and workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied.\\n- `python3 tests/test_documentation.py`: 12 tests passed after the documentation update.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed before the code commit.\\n- `full-check.log`: the required full check failed in the Rust wrapper. It stopped before its Node and Python steps.\\n- Rust wrapper totals: 1119 passed, one failed, across 20 reported test groups. This is not a passing workspace result.\\n- `python-check.log`: the separate full Python runner reported 86 files, with 62 passing and 24 failing.\\n\\nAll temporary roots were placed under `target/tmp/tinkery-TEST-build` to respect the checkout-only write boundary.\\nThat layout conflicts with fixtures that require output outside a repository or expect launch outside Git.\\nThe Rust failure is `tests::a_live_limit_counts_both_calls_of_a_send_and_records_the_run` in `examples/think_eval`.\\nIts error is `Live output stays outside the repository and the operator's Seed Me and Tinkery data.`\\n\\nSeveral Python failures show the enclosing checkout as the launch repository.\\nOther failures include changed garden-key expectations, long-path display, label saving and launch-guard behavior.\\nTheir individual causes are not all established. Do not classify every failure as an environment failure.\\nThe complete failing-file list and terminal output remain in `python-check.log`.\\n\\nAn initial separate Python-runner attempt refused the real HOME before launching its checks.\\nThe retained Python log comes from the later attempt with a checkout-local TEST HOME.\\n\\n### Confirmed-goal probe blocker\\n\\nProblem: the faulty confirmed-goal probe stops before it reaches the intended assertion.\\nGoal: prove the regression fails when saving a thought creates a confirmed goal session.\\n\\nThree attempts failed:\\n\\n1. A hand-written terminal declaration failed with `Invalid terminal confirmation declaration or action.`\\n2. The valid terminal constructor reached saving, but returned `The goal save could not be verified. Inspect the recovery session before retrying.`\\n3. A first-line goal instead of the raw multiline goal returned the same save-verification error.\\n\\nBoth final attempts passed an empty context to `Affirmed`.\\nThe lower-level ledger refusal was not exposed, so its cause remains unknown.\\nI stopped further fixes after the third attempt. `probe-failure.log` retains the final failure.\\n\\n`scripts/probe-thoughts.py` restores the original source files and rebuilds in its finalizer.\\nIts full command still fails at this first mutation.\\nThe two independent mutations passed when run separately, without changing the script.\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\nKeep this candidate blocked from acceptance.\\n\\n1. Inspect the lower-level refusal before another confirmed-goal mutation attempt. Then prove the intended assertion fails.\\n2. Establish baseline failures under the permitted TEST-root layout. Obtain permission before using roots outside this checkout.\\n3. Resolve actual regressions and run the full required checks again on committed work.\\n4. Obtain independent review, then continue with the run's verification and acceptance gates.\\n\\nThe approved brief, checklist and step contract were not edited.\\nThe generated `AGENTS.md` block and stage/step runtime files were already uncommitted at entry and remain untouched.\\nNo live endpoint requests, real audio recording, delegation, toolchain changes or Pi infrastructure edits occurred.\\nEvery terminal process started by the focused journeys was closed. No local server was started.\\n\"}\n==> text 3/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Tend and handoff\\n\\nTend holds saved goals and raw repository thoughts; [Shape](#shape) asks its questions with an explicit\\nmodel and budget.\\n\\n## Receipt\\n\\nExplicit successful saving shows `Saved.`, the exact frozen goal block and\\n`Next: shape it into a seed in Shape.`\\n\\n- `s open in tend` opens this session's detail, not the garden.\\n- Esc returns to the menu, including from standalone Think.\\n\\nNothing launches, opens a browser, pastes into a harness or starts implementation.\\nPaths belong in F1 then `h`, with the [think record](think.md#think-record) below\\nthe session path. If recording fails, the goal stays saved; help and a muted receipt\\nnotice disclose the gap. If only reading context was rejected, the successful receipt says\\n`Reading sequence wasn't saved; F1 then h shows why.` The path and full reason remain in\\ntechnical details and the plain-text exit receipt. Notices wrap without clipping in receipt and detail.\\nThe plain-text exit receipt may include recovery locations. Its next step is read\\nfrom the session at exit, through the shared verifier: a verified confirmed seed\\npoints to Approve, a draft to confirming in Shape, and a goal without a seed to\\nshaping. An unverifiable or unreadable session points to checking in Shape, never\\nclaims readiness; other ended sessions are named as ended.\\n\\n## Tend: garden and detail\\n\\nIn this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\\nthe repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\\ncall and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\\n`v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\\n`g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\\nThink goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\\nThoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\\n\\nThoughts use private atomic files under the captured Tend link root, separate from\\nsessions and goal confirmation records. Filenames bind the exact repository path\\nand exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\\nIdentical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\\nWhitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\\nempty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\\nnever edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\\n\\nInside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\\norigin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\\n`a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\\nall goals show without a toggle. Unknown, missing, older or conflicting records\\nnever guess a repo; those goals remain under all. An empty repo view still offers\\n`a`. If any active goal lacks attributable repo information, say `N goals have no\\nreadable repo record. Press a for all goals.`, not that this repo has no goals.\\nExplicit no-repo records are known non-matches; older records without repo\\ninformation are unknown. Only with no unknown active goals or unreadable sessions\\nmay an empty repo view say `No active goals are recorded for this repo.` With\\nunreadable sessions, say `N saved records couldn't be read; this repo may have\\nactive goals. Press a for all goals.` Ended counts remain visible. Reopening Tend\\nstarts with this repo again; explicit receipt or Shape returns still open the\\nexact saved goal, switching to all if necessary.\\n\\nFiltering reads existing records on discovery's worker, never during painting,\\nand writes nothing. Legacy discovery enumerates the Think record root once and\\nreads each JSON record at most once, rebuilding an in-memory attribution index;\\nrefreshes never reuse an earlier index. It shares history's strict validation and\\nrechecks session identity and goal across the scan. Malformed or unsupported files\\nmake every origin unknown; duplicate paths and matching schema-1 records refuse\\nattribution, never choose a winner. The index keeps paths, identities, exact goals\\nand origins, not turns or checks; the 16 MiB per-file limit remains, with no total\\nindex-size cap. Links, identity checks and readiness still use every readable\\nsession, including other repos and ended goals. Use all to link across repos;\\n`a` does nothing during linking, detail, history, help or pending/failed reads.\\n\\nTend displays the visible goals in one static graph, without paging or node cap.\\nEqual hollow Braille rings mean size is unknown; no sizes or merges are known.\\nNeeds lines join only active, uniquely identified endpoints. Missing, ambiguous or\\nended endpoints draw no line; the selected-line summary still names them. Straight\\nlines leave gaps around unrelated rings, never implied junctions or routed paths.\\nExisting sessions stay read-only; linking writes only Tend's store.\\n\\nEnded sessions are omitted. `N ended not shown` and\\n`Links couldn't be read. F1 then h for details.` share the muted incomplete-read\\nrow, joined by ` · `, even with no active goals, and survive navigation. An\\nunreadable-links refusal replaces, rather than repeats, the note. When an empty\\nview's body reports unreadable sessions, the footer keeps ended and link notes\\nwithout repeating that count. This applies to repo and all-goals views, including\\noutside a repository. An incomplete empty all-goals view says `N saved records\\ncouldn't be read, so nothing can be listed. Esc goes back.`, never `No active goals`.\\nOnly when every session was readable and ended, say `No active goals. N ended not\\nshown. Confirm a goal in think to start one.`, not that no sessions exist.\\n\\nLabels use the first saved-goal line, including unstructured goals. They sit above\\nor below rings, clipped with `…` or omitted rather than overlapping or interleaving.\\nThe selected label gets space first and always appears, prefixed `› `; its label\\nand ring are bold, jade with colour. Other labels are muted and rings use ink;\\nnone is italic.\\n\\nThe selected-line footer shows the first goal line in ink, status and relative time\\nmuted, then needs and readiness, e.g. `needs Local records · ready`.\\nValid offsets determine age and order. Timestamp syntax stays unchanged; invalid\\ndates and pre-epoch values remain `time unknown`.\\nUnresolved ids say `1 need not found` or `N needs not found`; no needs adds nothing.\\nShort summaries retain status and time. If these crowd the headline, show the\\nheadline, readiness and `F1 needs`; scrollable Help retains full titles. Ambiguous source\\nidentity says `readiness unknown` and attributes no needs. Refusals use the blank\\nrow before the key bar.\\n\\n| Input | Action |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Right, Down or `j`; Left, Up or `k` | Select next or previous in discovery's newest-first order, clamped; not graph neighbours. |\\n| Enter | Open detail. |\\n| `+` or `=`; `-` | Zoom in; zoom out. |\\n| `H J K L` | Pan left, down, up or right. |\\n| Left press on a ring or label | Select its exact session path; a second press within 500 ms opens it. |\\n| Drag a ring or label; drag empty space; scroll | Move the goal; pan; zoom. |\\n\\nThe key bar is `↑↓←→ move   enter open   l link   esc back` (fits 80 columns).\\nSelection pans offscreen goals into view without resetting zoom. Help, detail,\\nhistory, reading, empty and unavailable states ignore graph input.\\n\\nGraf uses deterministic identity-ordered slots adapted to the canvas, initially\\nat least 12 columns × 6 rows apart, without a physics thread. Crowded gardens\\nrequire navigation, panning or zooming, not simultaneous labels. Moving, panning\\nand zooming write nothing. Refresh preserves positions and viewport for an unchanged\\ngr…6969 tokens truncated…e intake status without `viewer`, `snapshot` or\\n`snapshot_current`; `tinkery seed checks DIR` prints the strict check records. Both are read-only.\\n\\nShape copies no intake command. [Approve](approve.md) owns the one command that\\ncreates a run in the named checkout and imports the seed, so a seed has one handoff\\nline and no placeholder to replace (#466). Seed ready points there; choosing or\\ncreating an SDLC run stays outside Shape.\\n\\n### The screen\\n\\n- Under `tinkery › shape` and `?`, content begins at the body top, at most 76 columns\\n  wide. The goal headline or draft, then stage, precedes words, notices and `Next:`.\\n  Overflow scrolls while the words box and cursor, or running status, stay visible,\\n  occupying at most half the body. Cursor following survives long or wrapped\\n  words and resize. Readings (seed plus review or feedback, and So far) must stay under 60,000 bytes; otherwise Shape refuses without confirming or changing anything.\\n  An empty reading viewport cannot mark a draft read.\\n  Only overflow offers `pgup/dn read` while editing or `↑↓ scroll`\\n  otherwise; overflowing questions shorten the save key to `F2 save + look`.\\n  Seed `Nothing found` stays beside words. Crowded bars reduce gaps to two spaces,\\n  never cut Esc.\\n- **So far** (from F1) is a full help-like page without a key bar: the entire confirmed\\n  goal unchanged, then settled `label: answer` decisions in ledger order. Only\\n  `user` authority shows `(you)`; others show their authority, e.g. `(delegated)`.\\n  Open questions follow in ledger order; held questions say `waits for:` with the earlier\\n  answer labels they need. All current-question findings follow, unchanged and in recorded order. Esc\\n  closes it; ↑↓ scrolls. The fixed last row says `↑↓ scroll · esc close`.\\n  It accepts no words, appears after a read, never during a step; F1 lists it.\\n- Say the next step once: omit `Next:` when the key bar names the stage action;\\n  other states and failure notices keep exactly one.\\n- Words boxes use ratatui-textarea, titled `your answer`, `your words`, `your teach-back`, `your change` or `Folder:`.\\n  Arrows, Home, End, Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right move the cursor; Shift selects.\\n  Ctrl+W or Alt+Backspace deletes a word; Enter inserts a newline except at seed confirmation; Ctrl+U undoes\\n  and Ctrl+R redoes. PgUp and PgDn scroll only the reading, a view less one row. Pasted CR and CRLF\\n  display as breaks; edits preserve untouched raw endings. Under seed words, say seed confirmation is not approval to build.\\n- Running steps keep label, question and typed words muted, with one status\\n  (`Saving your answer.`, then `Answer saved. Looking in NAME for the next question.`),\\n  elapsed seconds and `esc stop`. F1 says a step is running.\\n- Shape opens **Tink Contract rN** with proposed pass/fail checks. Each card shows its\\n  verification method, expected result and any proposed failure case from the review of\\n  those exact draft bytes. The remaining draft and supporting evidence follow.\\n  This display order changes neither `seed-contract.md` nor `tinkery seed` commands.\\n\\n### Answering and confirming\\n\\nConfigured drafting enables these actions; see [Model setup](menu.md#model-setup).\\nShape uses Think's\\n[one key map](think.md#help): F2 runs the action in the key bar, F1 numbers the rest.\\n\\n| Stage | Words | Key/action |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Flagged node | `your reason` | `F2 keep with reason`: keep the answer unchanged and revalidate, no model call |\\n| Flagged operator-answered decision | `replacement answer` after F1 **Revise** | `F2 save revision and look`: replace it, reopen settled dependents, then look |\\n| Current question | `your answer` | `F2 save + look`: save then one step |\\n| Current question | Reason, then revisit condition after F1 **Defer** | `F2 next field`, then `F2 save deferral`: publish deferred, then one step |\\n| Current question | None required | F1 **Delegate**: accept the grounded suggestion, then one step |\\n| No question or seed | None | `F2 look into the next question`: one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your words` | `F2 confirm seed rN`: confirm displayed revision when the words are exactly `confirm` |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your change` after F1 **Revise the draft** | `F2 save + redraft`: save the change as your settled decision, then one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your teach-back` after F1 **Teach back** | `F2 save + compare`: capture words and compare with the draft, one call; Esc restores confirmation words |\\n\\n- **Before confirmation:** the ledger computes the risk summary above confirming, including\\n  reversals detected from earlier settled answers, delegated and assumed choices,\\n  exact acceptance of suggestions, and accepted-versus-chosen-otherwise counts.\\n  Shape displays these words without its own checks or formatter.\\n- **Teach-back:** on a draft, F1's **Teach back** opens optional words about what will and won't be built,\\n  prefilled with any confirmation words already typed, editable in a separate box.\\n  F2 saves them verbatim, then compares in one call behind F2's shared budget,\\n  with no tools or repository access;\\n  opening, typing, help and cancelling do not save or call. Confirmation words remain\\n  untouched. The latest completed comparison for these draft bytes appears as guesses\\n  above the risk summary; mismatches are recorded verbatim and never block confirming.\\n  Failed comparisons retain captured words. Confirming without a completed comparison records\\n  `Skipped teach-back.` verbatim, after ordinary confirmation refusals. These append-only\\n  confirmed-goal receipts are bound to the revision and SHA-256 of draft bytes;\\n  confirmation digests cover them. They retain the existing receipt format and are\\n  interview records, not evidence changes or permission.\\n  F1 offers teach-back only on a draft.\\n- **Revise the draft (#614):** on a draft, F1's **Revise the draft** opens `your change`,\\n  prefilled with the confirmation words unless they are `confirm`, so a correction typed where\\n  `confirm` goes is never lost. F2 saves the words verbatim as a settled `change-to-rN` decision\\n  with the operator's authority, never a confirmation, then takes one drafting step behind F2's\\n  budget gate; the redraft lists the change under Decisions. Empty words or words that leave the\\n  change open are refused, saving nothing. Esc keeps the confirmation words untouched.\\n- **Defer:** F1's **Defer** opens the reason; F2 advances to the revisit condition; Tab switches\\n  between them. The form shows the question's gate: the operator alone decides it can wait.\\n  F2 on the condition saves both fields verbatim as `deferred`, never confirmed or settled.\\n  An answer, revision, revisit or delegated suggestion that is empty or only says the\\n  decision is open (\\\"not decided.\\\", \\\"TBD\\\") is refused, saving nothing and keeping the typed\\n  words, and points here (#594).\\n- **Answer deferred prerequisite:** an active Waiting session may offer one named deferred\\n  blocker in F1, selected by the ledger in its existing order. Its own prerequisites and\\n  predicate must be ready; the goal and flagged sessions never qualify. The form shows the\\n  original question, exact deferral reason and revisit condition. Opening, typing and Esc\\n  save nothing. F2 saves the exact answer with existing authorization, locking and stale-state\\n  checks, without a model call. Existing history preserves the prior deferral unchanged;\\n  dependent questions stay unanswered and follow ordinary ready ordering. No picker or\\n  automatic repair is provided. This keeps dependency selection and transitions in the\\n  ledger (architecture diagnostic 6).\\n- **Delegate:** F1's **Delegate** row is one choice, quoting that row as the authority source, saving the\\n  recorded suggestion unchanged with `delegated` authority and its supporting facts as evidence.\\n  Reply confidence is not appended to the recommendation or answer; the ledger never parses\\n  suggestion text.\\n  Missing facts or suggestion refuses without writing; type an answer instead.\\n- **Revise:** only flagged decisions answered by the operator (including delegated answers)\\n  offer F1 **Revise**. Flagged findings (facts and inferences) and the confirmed goal offer only\\n  keep-with-reason; Revise is not shown. There is no settled-answer picker: So far remains read-only.\\n  F2 saves exact replacement words with user authority; the ledger reopens every settled\\n  dependent with a reason naming the changed answer. Shape asks ready dependents one at a time\\n  before a new model question. Saving a revision uses F2's budget gate and next-step path:\\n  an already-recorded dependent is asked without a model call; otherwise one step investigates\\n  or replaces the older draft.\\n- Esc cancels a form without changing the original answer editor. Ledger refusals keep the\\n  question and both typed fields, show the first reason line and allow correction and retry.\\n  Required fields, delegated evidence, revision eligibility and cascading reopen belong only to\\n  the ledger; Shape adds no parallel rules. F1 lists only the actions allowed now.\\n- F2 saves exact answer bytes with `user` authority. Typing, paste, scrolling and\\n  help write nothing; held action keys never repeat. Letters, capitals and `?` remain words.\\n- The chosen harness runs one explicitly selected model with read-only tools (Pi's `read`,\\n  `grep`, `find`, `ls`; Claude Code's `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob` under `dontAsk`), no commands, in the [shown folder](#grounding-in-the-repository). Input includes\\n  the confirmed goal, attributable Think answers, every `found_so_far` finding and\\n  a model-only ledger view: findings appear only in `found_so_far`, not again as\\n  ledger fact nodes or copied decision evidence. Settled pre-mortem questions and answers stay\\n  once in their ledger decision nodes, not a second answer list. Goal provenance, including Think's\\n  original context, stays unchanged; stored ledgers are never trimmed. Replies require typed `found` entries (see\\n  [grounding](#grounding-in-the-repository)) plus a next question and suggestion, or seed summary, prose sections\\n  and separate typed `review` and final `checks` fields;\\n  anything else is a model error. Either reply may include optional `resolves`, a list of\\n  `{\\\"unknown\\\":\\\"FACT-ID\\\",\\\"resolved_by\\\":\\\"DECISION-ID\\\"}` links to an already-settled answer.\\n  Absence means no links; malformed or invalid links refuse the reply plainly, saving no\\n  findings, question or resolution. An answer saved before that step stays saved.\\n  [The ledger](shape-ledger.md#2-what-shape-writes) owns eligibility, history and reopening.\\n  A question may include optional `prerequisites`, a list\\n  of existing decision IDs, preserved unchanged (absent means `[]`). Facts belong in `supported_by`,\\n  not prerequisites. The ledger alone refuses unknown IDs, cycles, invalid lists and deferred\\n  prerequisites (a deferral is not a settled answer), saving no\\n  findings, question or assumptions from a refused reply. A held question stays open without\\n  becoming current; the ledger selects the next ready decision. Once its prerequisites settle,\\n  the held question is promoted before any model call. No reply can settle, skip or reorder\\n  earlier decisions. `src/shape/prompt.txt` has one rule per line.\\n  The decoder tolerates redundant closing braces only after one complete JSON object;\\n  it never reconstructs missing fields or chooses between multiple objects. Invalid\\n  JSON, a missing question and an unsupported reply kind have specific reasons.\\n  The step finds the blast radius and the ways to meet the goal before choosing to ask or draft.\\n- The launch allowance (saved calls or `--shape-budget CALLS`) defaults to zero; each step counts one before the model starts.\\n  With a current question and one run remaining, show `Drafting runs left this launch: 1 of M.`\\n  beside the answer editor before F2 spends it, using Think's shared budget wording.\\n  Budget policy stays behind Agent; Shape owns presentation (architecture diagnostics 3 and 6).\\n  Exhaustion refuses answer, defer, delegate, revision and teach-back before saving anything and explains how to allow calls.\\n- Tinkery, never the model, publishes answers and questions with the displayed version\\n  or the version at step start. Stale versions refuse, retain\\n  typed words and trigger a fresh read, never overwrite.\\n- Tinkery's bundled copy of the [seed contract source](https://github.com/jon-devlapaz/seed-me/blob/c9d766760dbeac0c05c92108165f9e968bec0a66/skills/seed-me/references/seed-contract.md)\\n  defines the artifact. Tinkery's ledger owns its canonical Full heading sequence;\\n  the reply fields and writer derive from that one layout. The model supplies\\n  `confirming` as an object: `You are confirming` contains exactly five non-empty\\n  summary lines, and each model-written prose section has its own string field named\\n  for the section, without heading syntax. Field order is immaterial. The summary\\n  covers goal, what gets built, what does not, the proposed first slice, and unknowns.\\n  Counts and reversal indicators belong to the ledger-computed confirmation summary.\\n  Drafting instructions retain names supplied\\n  in the confirmed goal or Think answers, including in the summary and knowledge\\n  map; a supplied tool name does not settle its executable path or invocation.\\n  Missing, blank, non-string or foreign fields\\n  refuse; prose cannot inject headings, fences, metadata or confirmation lines.\\n  Refusals name the rule and field, plus the offending line for structural text.\\n  A historical Markdown reply beginning `## You are confirming` is refused naming\\n  `confirming`, never with a generic format error.\\n  Shape attaches the bundled reference's section content guidance and check schema,\\n  not its instructions to write or paste artifact headings. The prompt defers to the\\n  generated field instructions, so there is no competing model-written layout.\\n  Tinkery writes every heading, `status: draft`, the goal-headline title,\\n  `revision: rN` one past the previous draft, and a separate `date:` line with the\\n  operator's local date (receipts stay UTC). An older writer can still increment the\\n  revision after rollback. Never replace a confirmed seed or draft with an open decision.\\n  Acceptance criteria, Decisions, Assumed and Evidence and uncertainty come only from\\n  recorded checks, decisions, assumptions and findings, in their canonical positions.\\n  Host-owned headings use LF; prose keeps its line endings. Ledger-owned blocks remain\\n  verbatim, with no extra wrappers. The exact generated title and origin-decision\\n  line treat goal comment markers as literal data during seed verification, only\\n  outside an existing comment. Their text and the confirmed goal remain unchanged;\\n  general heading and prose validation still refuse injected structure.\\n  Findings and question transport are unchanged.\\n- **Completion review runs within drafting**, with no extra call. Before producing a seed,\\n  the step compares settled decisions for contradictions and separates choices (`decided`)\\n  from observed completed work (`done`). Each model check carries its own non-empty\\n  `failure_case` string, including provisional and judge checks. The decoder removes this\\n  model-only field before canonical check validation and pairs it with that check's exact\\n  final statement; the model need not count a second list or copy statements (#469).\\n  A new blocker returns as a question, not a seed. The typed `review` object requires\\n  `contradictions`, `decided` and `done`. Older replies with ordered `review.failure_cases`\\n  strings still work strictly; mixed formats, missing cases and malformed cases refuse.\\n  Tinkery never duplicates, drops or invents cases to make coverage fit. Recorded clinic\\n  count mismatches and statement/case-object replies remain refusals.\\n  Saved check and review formats are unchanged. The ledger's `CompletionReview::validate`\\n\\n[Showing lines 1-716 of 1023 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=717 to continue.]\"}\n==> text 4/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Prove thought protections by introducing three faults, then restore sources and binary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT/'tests'))\\nimport test_launch\\n\\nTHOUGHT = ROOT/'src/tend/thought.rs'\\nCONNECTION = ROOT/'src/tend/connection.rs'\\nFAULTS = [\\n    ('confirmed-goal', THOUGHT, '        let path = self.file(words)?;', '''        crate::seed_me::Config::new(Some(root.parent().unwrap().join(\\\"sessions\\\"))).confirm_as(\\n            crate::seed_me::Affirmed {\\n                goal: words.lines().next().unwrap().trim().into(), outcome: String::new(), options: vec![], originals: vec![],\\n                context: String::new(), source: \\\"TEST faulty thought confirmation\\\".into(),\\n            },\\n            &crate::think_record::GoalConfirmation::terminal(Some(\\\"agent\\\"))?,\\n        )?;\\n        let path = self.file(words)?;''', 'A thought changed goal sessions'),\\n    ('changed-words', THOUGHT, '            words: words.into(),',\\n     '            words: words.trim().into(),', 'Saved words differ from typed words'),\\n    ('provider-source', CONNECTION, '        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));', '''        for entry in fs::read_dir(&self.store).map_err(|e| e.to_string())? {\\n            let path = entry.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.path();\\n            if path.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().starts_with(\\\"thought-\\\") {\\n                let thought: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(path).unwrap()).unwrap();\\n                if thought[\\\"repo\\\"] == serde_json::json!(self.repo) {\\n                    sources.push(Source { id: \\\"TEST-thought\\\".into(),\\n                        goal: thought[\\\"words\\\"].as_str().unwrap().into(), repo: self.repo.clone(),\\n                        status: \\\"active\\\".into() });\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));''', 'A thought reached the provider request'),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    env = test_launch.environment()\\n    output = ROOT/'target/thought-probes'\\n    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    originals = {p: p.read_text() for p in [THOUGHT, CONNECTION]}\\n\\n    def build():\\n        test_launch.run(['cargo', '+stable', 'build', '--locked', '--quiet'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n    try:\\n        for name, path, old, new, expected in FAULTS:\\n            source = originals[path]\\n            if source.count(old) != 1:\\n                raise SystemExit(f'{name}: mutation no longer matches exactly once')\\n            path.write_text(source.replace(old, new))\\n            try:\\n                build()\\n                result = test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env,\\n                                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)\\n                log = result.stdout + result.stderr\\n                (output/f'{name}.log').write_text(log)\\n                if result.returncode == 0 or expected not in log:\\n                    raise SystemExit(f'{name}: protection did not fail for the expected reason\\\\n{log}')\\n                print(f'{name}: rejected ({expected})', flush=True)\\n            finally:\\n                path.write_text(source)\\n    finally:\\n        for path, source in originals.items():\\n            path.write_text(source)\\n        build()\\n    test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    main()\\n\"}\n==> text 5/5 <==\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/thought-journeys.log\nscripts/probe-thoughts.py\nsrc/tend/thought.rs\ntests/tend_thought_terminal.py\n\n[Full output: /var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt (read with offset/limit)]"}],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9109159999970871},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9104169999991427},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":1.5290420000019367},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.5485420000004524},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","args":"{\"pattern\":\"*thought*\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":11.119833999997354}],"fullOutputPath":"/var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt"},"isError":false,"durationMs":49,"timestamp":1794733047304,"nestedCalls":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"scripts/probe-thoughts.py"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","status":"ok","arguments":{"pattern":"*thought*"},"durationMs":11}],"complete":true}}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe","name":"codemode","arguments":{"code":"for(const p of [\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\",\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\",\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"])text({path:p,content:await tools.read({path:p})});text(await tools.find({pattern:\"*thought*\"}));\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":1628,"output":97,"cacheRead":22016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":23741,"cost":{"input":0.0032559999999999998,"output":0.00097,"cacheRead":0.0022016,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0064276,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794733043906,"responseId":"resp_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f40d7887d18f65c4ff97d6ea98","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":3347,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe","toolName":"codemode","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16969)\nTotal output lines: 14\n\n==> text 1/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\",\"content\":\"# Repair brief for step build-fix (supervisor, 2026-11-15)\\n\\nRead this file first, then `03-build/output/handoff.md` from the first build step. The approved scope is unchanged: `brief.md` (issue #864).\\nCandidate under repair: commit `21277a3` plus `a33c440` on branch `issue-864-tend-thought`. You have at most 80 responses. Do the items in order.\\n\\n## Observed by the supervisor\\n\\n`python3 scripts/full-check.py` ran on `a33c440` with its normal temporary TEST HOME outside the checkout.\\nRust: all groups passed. Node: 39 passed. Lint and Clippy passed. Python: 84 of 86 files passed. Two files failed:\\n\\n1. `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, line 196, at 80×24:\\n   `AssertionError: Missing '↑↓←→ move   enter open   f connections   l link   esc back'`.\\n   The screen showed `arrows move   enter open   t thought   v read   f connect   l link   esc bac`.\\n   The existing key-bar labels were shortened, and the exit label is cut at 80 columns.\\n2. `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, line 146 (`edits_and_conflicts`): `AssertionError: Missing 'F2 find one connection'`. Cause not yet observed.\\n\\nThe first build's 24 Python failures came from TEST roots placed inside the checkout. Do not repeat that layout.\\n\\n## Repair items\\n\\n1. Key bar. Restore the existing garden key-bar text exactly, at every width the existing tests cover. Do not edit existing tests to fit new text.\\n   Yohaku Article 4 requires a legible exit: `esc back` must never be cut. Show the thought keys without shortening or displacing existing labels.\\n   The thought summary line already names `v read` and `t new thought`; when no thought exists, the `t` key still needs one visible, uncut place.\\n2. `tend_correction_terminal.py`. Reproduce the failure, find the observed cause, and fix that cause. Do not weaken the assertion.\\n3. Reversion probe for \\\"a thought is recorded as a confirmed goal\\\". The first builder failed three times with a hand-built `Affirmed`.\\n   Fresh approach: make the mutation call the existing public `shape::command::new_goal` (the `tinkery seed new` path), which already writes a\\n   confirmed goal session with no Think record. Prove the journey's assertion fails under that mutation, then restore the source and rebuild.\\n   `scripts/probe-thoughts.py` must run all three mutations in one command and exit zero only when each mutation is rejected.\\n4. Robustness, small: one malformed or foreign-format thought file must not hide the other thoughts. Show the readable ones and say how many could not be read.\\n   If this needs more than a small change inside `src/tend/thought.rs`, do not build it; report it instead.\\n\\n## Checks you run\\n\\n- Focused: `tests/tend_thought_terminal.py`, `tests/goal_confirmation_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_correction_terminal.py`, `tests/tend_terminal.py`,\\n  `tests/tend_connection_terminal.py`, `tests/test_documentation.py`, then `cargo +stable fmt --all -- --check` and Clippy with `-D warnings`.\\n- Full: `python3 scripts/full-check.py` from the checkout root, unchanged. It creates its own temporary TEST HOME in the system temporary directory.\\n  The supervisor permits that temporary write for this command only. Never point TEST roots at the checkout, the operator HOME or application stores.\\n- After the checks pass on committed work, mark each checklist item with `python3 _system/scripts/sdlc.py mark issue-864-tend-thought <id> passed --evidence <text>`.\\n  Mark an item `failed` or leave it unmarked when its evidence is missing. Do not run `verify`; the supervisor runs it.\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\nNo scope beyond #864. No provider calls, no subagents, no changes to the shared goal saver, session formats, Find connections input or the saved correction.\\nProduct-shape choices (key letters, the word \\\"thought\\\") stay as built; list any doubt in the report for the operator.\\nAfter two failed fixes of one defect, add logging and collect observations. After three, stop and report problem, goal and failed attempts.\\nCommit before you end. Write the report at the path in your step contract, result first, with counts for Rust, Node, Python files, journeys and probes.\\n\"}\n==> text 2/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Build handoff\\n\\n## Situation\\n\\nThe implementation is committed. The run is not ready for acceptance.\\nFull checks fail, and the confirmed-goal reversion probe remains incomplete.\\n\\n- Run ID: `d50e7a87-1232-43e5-a29a-0cbf2512c1ab`.\\n- Checkout: `/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/tinkery/issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Code candidate: `21277a33dc5d469c7ee9ad880fd013c8d31bd8ad`.\\n- Branch: `issue-864-tend-thought`.\\n- Approved input: `runs/issue-864-tend-thought/brief.md`, from issue #864.\\n- Issue body SHA-256: `29f447833355967617805c1fc76789f53c35598279aa8b5a4f7ba921cf6aa3b1`.\\n- This light run has no seed-contract binding in `run.json`.\\n- Step pin: `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium`. I did not change it.\\n- No PR, independent review, operator acceptance or SDLC verification receipt was created.\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nTend now keeps raw thoughts separately from saved goal sessions.\\n\\n- In the repository garden, `t` opens an exact-word editor.\\n- The editor displays the repository before `F2` saves without a model call.\\n- The garden labels saved entries as thoughts. `v` opens the local thought reader.\\n- Identical bytes in one repository produce one entry and an explicit duplicate notice.\\n- `g` opens the selected words in Think, unsent. Existing goal confirmation remains necessary.\\n- Thoughts cannot open Shape. Find connections still reads saved goals only.\\n- Thoughts use private atomic files in the existing Tend link root.\\n- The new format stores only `schema`, `repo` and `words`.\\n- Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes. They have no edit or delete action.\\n\\nThe exact-word editor moved from `src/shape/words.rs` to shared `src/words.rs`.\\nIts six existing tests moved unchanged. No shared goal saver or session format changed.\\nNo storage service, provider endpoint or migration was added.\\n\\nThe architecture diagnostics affected are 1, 3, 6 and 7.\\nThought persistence stays inside Tend. The menu alone connects a thought to Think.\\nShape and Tend share one editor rather than separate copies of its line-ending rules.\\n\\nSkills read in full:\\n\\n- `principle-build-the-lever` led to a repeatable PTY test and `scripts/probe-thoughts.py`.\\n- `unslop` kept the documentation and notices direct about saving, confirmation and failure.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n### Checked acceptance evidence\\n\\n`tests/tend_thought_terminal.py` passed on the committed code candidate.\\nIt runs six top-level journeys across 80×24 and 100×30 terminals, without colour.\\nIt launches 12 terminal processes with temporary TEST roots.\\nSave, restart, duplicate, cancellation and store-refusal actions make no provider requests.\\nConnection and goal-confirmation checks use local executable stubs, not live providers.\\n\\n1. Checked exact received UTF-8 bytes after explicit saving, including CRLF, CR, tabs, Unicode and trailing whitespace.\\n2. Checked restart discovery, thought labels and isolation between two repositories.\\n3. Checked unchanged goal-session files and confirmation records after thought saves. Pressing `s` does not open Shape.\\n4. Checked Find connections succeeds with thoughts present. Its request contains only the two original goal sources.\\n5. Checked duplicate saving leaves one record and displays `Thought already saved. One entry.`\\n6. Checked the existing Think review and typed confirmation save a goal. The first original equals the thought bytes.\\n7. Checked cancellation and an unwritable store at both sizes. A failed save keeps the words in the editor.\\n8. Partially checked. Changed-word and provider-source mutations fail their intended assertions. The confirmed-goal mutation is not proven.\\n\\nEach saved thought file also passed a `0600` permission check.\\nThese checks prove mechanics with synthetic words. They do not establish operator acceptance or real-data usefulness.\\n\\n### Check results\\n\\nThe logs beside this report retain the observed results.\\n\\n- `thought-journeys.log`: the focused journeys passed again after the code commit.\\n- `independent-probes.log`: changed-word and provider-source faults were rejected. Sources and binary were restored, then journeys passed.\\n- `node-check.log`: 39 Node tests passed, zero failed.\\n- `lint-check.log`: formatting and workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied.\\n- `python3 tests/test_documentation.py`: 12 tests passed after the documentation update.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed before the code commit.\\n- `full-check.log`: the required full check failed in the Rust wrapper. It stopped before its Node and Python steps.\\n- Rust wrapper totals: 1119 passed, one failed, across 20 reported test groups. This is not a passing workspace result.\\n- `python-check.log`: the separate full Python runner reported 86 files, with 62 passing and 24 failing.\\n\\nAll temporary roots were placed under `target/tmp/tinkery-TEST-build` to respect the checkout-only write boundary.\\nThat layout conflicts with fixtures that require output outside a repository or expect launch outside Git.\\nThe Rust failure is `tests::a_live_limit_counts_both_calls_of_a_send_and_records_the_run` in `examples/think_eval`.\\nIts error is `Live output stays outside the repository and the operator's Seed Me and Tinkery data.`\\n\\nSeveral Python failures show the enclosing checkout as the launch repository.\\nOther failures include changed garden-key expectations, long-path display, label saving and launch-guard behavior.\\nTheir individual causes are not all established. Do not classify every failure as an environment failure.\\nThe complete failing-file list and terminal output remain in `python-check.log`.\\n\\nAn initial separate Python-runner attempt refused the real HOME before launching its checks.\\nThe retained Python log comes from the later attempt with a checkout-local TEST HOME.\\n\\n### Confirmed-goal probe blocker\\n\\nProblem: the faulty confirmed-goal probe stops before it reaches the intended assertion.\\nGoal: prove the regression fails when saving a thought creates a confirmed goal session.\\n\\nThree attempts failed:\\n\\n1. A hand-written terminal declaration failed with `Invalid terminal confirmation declaration or action.`\\n2. The valid terminal constructor reached saving, but returned `The goal save could not be verified. Inspect the recovery session before retrying.`\\n3. A first-line goal instead of the raw multiline goal returned the same save-verification error.\\n\\nBoth final attempts passed an empty context to `Affirmed`.\\nThe lower-level ledger refusal was not exposed, so its cause remains unknown.\\nI stopped further fixes after the third attempt. `probe-failure.log` retains the final failure.\\n\\n`scripts/probe-thoughts.py` restores the original source files and rebuilds in its finalizer.\\nIts full command still fails at this first mutation.\\nThe two independent mutations passed when run separately, without changing the script.\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\nKeep this candidate blocked from acceptance.\\n\\n1. Inspect the lower-level refusal before another confirmed-goal mutation attempt. Then prove the intended assertion fails.\\n2. Establish baseline failures under the permitted TEST-root layout. Obtain permission before using roots outside this checkout.\\n3. Resolve actual regressions and run the full required checks again on committed work.\\n4. Obtain independent review, then continue with the run's verification and acceptance gates.\\n\\nThe approved brief, checklist and step contract were not edited.\\nThe generated `AGENTS.md` block and stage/step runtime files were already uncommitted at entry and remain untouched.\\nNo live endpoint requests, real audio recording, delegation, toolchain changes or Pi infrastructure edits occurred.\\nEvery terminal process started by the focused journeys was closed. No local server was started.\\n\"}\n==> text 3/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"content\":\"# Tend and handoff\\n\\nTend holds saved goals and raw repository thoughts; [Shape](#shape) asks its questions with an explicit\\nmodel and budget.\\n\\n## Receipt\\n\\nExplicit successful saving shows `Saved.`, the exact frozen goal block and\\n`Next: shape it into a seed in Shape.`\\n\\n- `s open in tend` opens this session's detail, not the garden.\\n- Esc returns to the menu, including from standalone Think.\\n\\nNothing launches, opens a browser, pastes into a harness or starts implementation.\\nPaths belong in F1 then `h`, with the [think record](think.md#think-record) below\\nthe session path. If recording fails, the goal stays saved; help and a muted receipt\\nnotice disclose the gap. If only reading context was rejected, the successful receipt says\\n`Reading sequence wasn't saved; F1 then h shows why.` The path and full reason remain in\\ntechnical details and the plain-text exit receipt. Notices wrap without clipping in receipt and detail.\\nThe plain-text exit receipt may include recovery locations. Its next step is read\\nfrom the session at exit, through the shared verifier: a verified confirmed seed\\npoints to Approve, a draft to confirming in Shape, and a goal without a seed to\\nshaping. An unverifiable or unreadable session points to checking in Shape, never\\nclaims readiness; other ended sessions are named as ended.\\n\\n## Tend: garden and detail\\n\\nIn this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\\nthe repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\\ncall and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\\n`v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\\n`g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\\nThink goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\\nThoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\\n\\nThoughts use private atomic files under the captured Tend link root, separate from\\nsessions and goal confirmation records. Filenames bind the exact repository path\\nand exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\\nIdentical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\\nWhitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\\nempty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\\nnever edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\\n\\nInside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\\norigin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\\n`a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\\nall goals show without a toggle. Unknown, missing, older or conflicting records\\nnever guess a repo; those goals remain under all. An empty repo view still offers\\n`a`. If any active goal lacks attributable repo information, say `N goals have no\\nreadable repo record. Press a for all goals.`, not that this repo has no goals.\\nExplicit no-repo records are known non-matches; older records without repo\\ninformation are unknown. Only with no unknown active goals or unreadable sessions\\nmay an empty repo view say `No active goals are recorded for this repo.` With\\nunreadable sessions, say `N saved records couldn't be read; this repo may have\\nactive goals. Press a for all goals.` Ended counts remain visible. Reopening Tend\\nstarts with this repo again; explicit receipt or Shape returns still open the\\nexact saved goal, switching to all if necessary.\\n\\nFiltering reads existing records on discovery's worker, never during painting,\\nand writes nothing. Legacy discovery enumerates the Think record root once and\\nreads each JSON record at most once, rebuilding an in-memory attribution index;\\nrefreshes never reuse an earlier index. It shares history's strict validation and\\nrechecks session identity and goal across the scan. Malformed or unsupported files\\nmake every origin unknown; duplicate paths and matching schema-1 records refuse\\nattribution, never choose a winner. The index keeps paths, identities, exact goals\\nand origins, not turns or checks; the 16 MiB per-file limit remains, with no total\\nindex-size cap. Links, identity checks and readiness still use every readable\\nsession, including other repos and ended goals. Use all to link across repos;\\n`a` does nothing during linking, detail, history, help or pending/failed reads.\\n\\nTend displays the visible goals in one static graph, without paging or node cap.\\nEqual hollow Braille rings mean size is unknown; no sizes or merges are known.\\nNeeds lines join only active, uniquely identified endpoints. Missing, ambiguous or\\nended endpoints draw no line; the selected-line summary still names them. Straight\\nlines leave gaps around unrelated rings, never implied junctions or routed paths.\\nExisting sessions stay read-only; linking writes only Tend's store.\\n\\nEnded sessions are omitted. `N ended not shown` and\\n`Links couldn't be read. F1 then h for details.` share the muted incomplete-read\\nrow, joined by ` · `, even with no active goals, and survive navigation. An\\nunreadable-links refusal replaces, rather than repeats, the note. When an empty\\nview's body reports unreadable sessions, the footer keeps ended and link notes\\nwithout repeating that count. This applies to repo and all-goals views, including\\noutside a repository. An incomplete empty all-goals view says `N saved records\\ncouldn't be read, so nothing can be listed. Esc goes back.`, never `No active goals`.\\nOnly when every session was readable and ended, say `No active goals. N ended not\\nshown. Confirm a goal in think to start one.`, not that no sessions exist.\\n\\nLabels use the first saved-goal line, including unstructured goals. They sit above\\nor below rings, clipped with `…` or omitted rather than overlapping or interleaving.\\nThe selected label gets space first and always appears, prefixed `› `; its label\\nand ring are bold, jade with colour. Other labels are muted and rings use ink;\\nnone is italic.\\n\\nThe selected-line footer shows the first goal line in ink, status and relative time\\nmuted, then needs and readiness, e.g. `needs Local records · ready`.\\nValid offsets determine age and order. Timestamp syntax stays unchanged; invalid\\ndates and pre-epoch values remain `time unknown`.\\nUnresolved ids say `1 need not found` or `N needs not found`; no needs adds nothing.\\nShort summaries retain status and time. If these crowd the headline, show the\\nheadline, readiness and `F1 needs`; scrollable Help retains full titles. Ambiguous source\\nidentity says `readiness unknown` and attributes no needs. Refusals use the blank\\nrow before the key bar.\\n\\n| Input | Action |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Right, Down or `j`; Left, Up or `k` | Select next or previous in discovery's newest-first order, clamped; not graph neighbours. |\\n| Enter | Open detail. |\\n| `+` or `=`; `-` | Zoom in; zoom out. |\\n| `H J K L` | Pan left, down, up or right. |\\n| Left press on a ring or label | Select its exact session path; a second press within 500 ms opens it. |\\n| Drag a ring or label; drag empty space; scroll | Move the goal; pan; zoom. |\\n\\nThe key bar is `↑↓←→ move   enter open   l link   esc back` (fits 80 columns).\\nSelection pans offscreen goals into view without resetting zoom. Help, detail,\\nhistory, reading, empty and unavailable states ignore graph input.\\n\\nGraf uses deterministic identity-ordered slots adapted to the canvas, initially\\nat least 12 columns × 6 rows apart, without a physics thread. Crowded gardens\\nrequire navigation, panning or zooming, not simultaneous labels. Moving, panning\\nand zooming write nothing. Refresh preserves positions and viewport for an unchanged\\ngr…6969 tokens truncated…e intake status without `viewer`, `snapshot` or\\n`snapshot_current`; `tinkery seed checks DIR` prints the strict check records. Both are read-only.\\n\\nShape copies no intake command. [Approve](approve.md) owns the one command that\\ncreates a run in the named checkout and imports the seed, so a seed has one handoff\\nline and no placeholder to replace (#466). Seed ready points there; choosing or\\ncreating an SDLC run stays outside Shape.\\n\\n### The screen\\n\\n- Under `tinkery › shape` and `?`, content begins at the body top, at most 76 columns\\n  wide. The goal headline or draft, then stage, precedes words, notices and `Next:`.\\n  Overflow scrolls while the words box and cursor, or running status, stay visible,\\n  occupying at most half the body. Cursor following survives long or wrapped\\n  words and resize. Readings (seed plus review or feedback, and So far) must stay under 60,000 bytes; otherwise Shape refuses without confirming or changing anything.\\n  An empty reading viewport cannot mark a draft read.\\n  Only overflow offers `pgup/dn read` while editing or `↑↓ scroll`\\n  otherwise; overflowing questions shorten the save key to `F2 save + look`.\\n  Seed `Nothing found` stays beside words. Crowded bars reduce gaps to two spaces,\\n  never cut Esc.\\n- **So far** (from F1) is a full help-like page without a key bar: the entire confirmed\\n  goal unchanged, then settled `label: answer` decisions in ledger order. Only\\n  `user` authority shows `(you)`; others show their authority, e.g. `(delegated)`.\\n  Open questions follow in ledger order; held questions say `waits for:` with the earlier\\n  answer labels they need. All current-question findings follow, unchanged and in recorded order. Esc\\n  closes it; ↑↓ scrolls. The fixed last row says `↑↓ scroll · esc close`.\\n  It accepts no words, appears after a read, never during a step; F1 lists it.\\n- Say the next step once: omit `Next:` when the key bar names the stage action;\\n  other states and failure notices keep exactly one.\\n- Words boxes use ratatui-textarea, titled `your answer`, `your words`, `your teach-back`, `your change` or `Folder:`.\\n  Arrows, Home, End, Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right move the cursor; Shift selects.\\n  Ctrl+W or Alt+Backspace deletes a word; Enter inserts a newline except at seed confirmation; Ctrl+U undoes\\n  and Ctrl+R redoes. PgUp and PgDn scroll only the reading, a view less one row. Pasted CR and CRLF\\n  display as breaks; edits preserve untouched raw endings. Under seed words, say seed confirmation is not approval to build.\\n- Running steps keep label, question and typed words muted, with one status\\n  (`Saving your answer.`, then `Answer saved. Looking in NAME for the next question.`),\\n  elapsed seconds and `esc stop`. F1 says a step is running.\\n- Shape opens **Tink Contract rN** with proposed pass/fail checks. Each card shows its\\n  verification method, expected result and any proposed failure case from the review of\\n  those exact draft bytes. The remaining draft and supporting evidence follow.\\n  This display order changes neither `seed-contract.md` nor `tinkery seed` commands.\\n\\n### Answering and confirming\\n\\nConfigured drafting enables these actions; see [Model setup](menu.md#model-setup).\\nShape uses Think's\\n[one key map](think.md#help): F2 runs the action in the key bar, F1 numbers the rest.\\n\\n| Stage | Words | Key/action |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Flagged node | `your reason` | `F2 keep with reason`: keep the answer unchanged and revalidate, no model call |\\n| Flagged operator-answered decision | `replacement answer` after F1 **Revise** | `F2 save revision and look`: replace it, reopen settled dependents, then look |\\n| Current question | `your answer` | `F2 save + look`: save then one step |\\n| Current question | Reason, then revisit condition after F1 **Defer** | `F2 next field`, then `F2 save deferral`: publish deferred, then one step |\\n| Current question | None required | F1 **Delegate**: accept the grounded suggestion, then one step |\\n| No question or seed | None | `F2 look into the next question`: one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your words` | `F2 confirm seed rN`: confirm displayed revision when the words are exactly `confirm` |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your change` after F1 **Revise the draft** | `F2 save + redraft`: save the change as your settled decision, then one step |\\n| Draft replacing goal | `your teach-back` after F1 **Teach back** | `F2 save + compare`: capture words and compare with the draft, one call; Esc restores confirmation words |\\n\\n- **Before confirmation:** the ledger computes the risk summary above confirming, including\\n  reversals detected from earlier settled answers, delegated and assumed choices,\\n  exact acceptance of suggestions, and accepted-versus-chosen-otherwise counts.\\n  Shape displays these words without its own checks or formatter.\\n- **Teach-back:** on a draft, F1's **Teach back** opens optional words about what will and won't be built,\\n  prefilled with any confirmation words already typed, editable in a separate box.\\n  F2 saves them verbatim, then compares in one call behind F2's shared budget,\\n  with no tools or repository access;\\n  opening, typing, help and cancelling do not save or call. Confirmation words remain\\n  untouched. The latest completed comparison for these draft bytes appears as guesses\\n  above the risk summary; mismatches are recorded verbatim and never block confirming.\\n  Failed comparisons retain captured words. Confirming without a completed comparison records\\n  `Skipped teach-back.` verbatim, after ordinary confirmation refusals. These append-only\\n  confirmed-goal receipts are bound to the revision and SHA-256 of draft bytes;\\n  confirmation digests cover them. They retain the existing receipt format and are\\n  interview records, not evidence changes or permission.\\n  F1 offers teach-back only on a draft.\\n- **Revise the draft (#614):** on a draft, F1's **Revise the draft** opens `your change`,\\n  prefilled with the confirmation words unless they are `confirm`, so a correction typed where\\n  `confirm` goes is never lost. F2 saves the words verbatim as a settled `change-to-rN` decision\\n  with the operator's authority, never a confirmation, then takes one drafting step behind F2's\\n  budget gate; the redraft lists the change under Decisions. Empty words or words that leave the\\n  change open are refused, saving nothing. Esc keeps the confirmation words untouched.\\n- **Defer:** F1's **Defer** opens the reason; F2 advances to the revisit condition; Tab switches\\n  between them. The form shows the question's gate: the operator alone decides it can wait.\\n  F2 on the condition saves both fields verbatim as `deferred`, never confirmed or settled.\\n  An answer, revision, revisit or delegated suggestion that is empty or only says the\\n  decision is open (\\\"not decided.\\\", \\\"TBD\\\") is refused, saving nothing and keeping the typed\\n  words, and points here (#594).\\n- **Answer deferred prerequisite:** an active Waiting session may offer one named deferred\\n  blocker in F1, selected by the ledger in its existing order. Its own prerequisites and\\n  predicate must be ready; the goal and flagged sessions never qualify. The form shows the\\n  original question, exact deferral reason and revisit condition. Opening, typing and Esc\\n  save nothing. F2 saves the exact answer with existing authorization, locking and stale-state\\n  checks, without a model call. Existing history preserves the prior deferral unchanged;\\n  dependent questions stay unanswered and follow ordinary ready ordering. No picker or\\n  automatic repair is provided. This keeps dependency selection and transitions in the\\n  ledger (architecture diagnostic 6).\\n- **Delegate:** F1's **Delegate** row is one choice, quoting that row as the authority source, saving the\\n  recorded suggestion unchanged with `delegated` authority and its supporting facts as evidence.\\n  Reply confidence is not appended to the recommendation or answer; the ledger never parses\\n  suggestion text.\\n  Missing facts or suggestion refuses without writing; type an answer instead.\\n- **Revise:** only flagged decisions answered by the operator (including delegated answers)\\n  offer F1 **Revise**. Flagged findings (facts and inferences) and the confirmed goal offer only\\n  keep-with-reason; Revise is not shown. There is no settled-answer picker: So far remains read-only.\\n  F2 saves exact replacement words with user authority; the ledger reopens every settled\\n  dependent with a reason naming the changed answer. Shape asks ready dependents one at a time\\n  before a new model question. Saving a revision uses F2's budget gate and next-step path:\\n  an already-recorded dependent is asked without a model call; otherwise one step investigates\\n  or replaces the older draft.\\n- Esc cancels a form without changing the original answer editor. Ledger refusals keep the\\n  question and both typed fields, show the first reason line and allow correction and retry.\\n  Required fields, delegated evidence, revision eligibility and cascading reopen belong only to\\n  the ledger; Shape adds no parallel rules. F1 lists only the actions allowed now.\\n- F2 saves exact answer bytes with `user` authority. Typing, paste, scrolling and\\n  help write nothing; held action keys never repeat. Letters, capitals and `?` remain words.\\n- The chosen harness runs one explicitly selected model with read-only tools (Pi's `read`,\\n  `grep`, `find`, `ls`; Claude Code's `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob` under `dontAsk`), no commands, in the [shown folder](#grounding-in-the-repository). Input includes\\n  the confirmed goal, attributable Think answers, every `found_so_far` finding and\\n  a model-only ledger view: findings appear only in `found_so_far`, not again as\\n  ledger fact nodes or copied decision evidence. Settled pre-mortem questions and answers stay\\n  once in their ledger decision nodes, not a second answer list. Goal provenance, including Think's\\n  original context, stays unchanged; stored ledgers are never trimmed. Replies require typed `found` entries (see\\n  [grounding](#grounding-in-the-repository)) plus a next question and suggestion, or seed summary, prose sections\\n  and separate typed `review` and final `checks` fields;\\n  anything else is a model error. Either reply may include optional `resolves`, a list of\\n  `{\\\"unknown\\\":\\\"FACT-ID\\\",\\\"resolved_by\\\":\\\"DECISION-ID\\\"}` links to an already-settled answer.\\n  Absence means no links; malformed or invalid links refuse the reply plainly, saving no\\n  findings, question or resolution. An answer saved before that step stays saved.\\n  [The ledger](shape-ledger.md#2-what-shape-writes) owns eligibility, history and reopening.\\n  A question may include optional `prerequisites`, a list\\n  of existing decision IDs, preserved unchanged (absent means `[]`). Facts belong in `supported_by`,\\n  not prerequisites. The ledger alone refuses unknown IDs, cycles, invalid lists and deferred\\n  prerequisites (a deferral is not a settled answer), saving no\\n  findings, question or assumptions from a refused reply. A held question stays open without\\n  becoming current; the ledger selects the next ready decision. Once its prerequisites settle,\\n  the held question is promoted before any model call. No reply can settle, skip or reorder\\n  earlier decisions. `src/shape/prompt.txt` has one rule per line.\\n  The decoder tolerates redundant closing braces only after one complete JSON object;\\n  it never reconstructs missing fields or chooses between multiple objects. Invalid\\n  JSON, a missing question and an unsupported reply kind have specific reasons.\\n  The step finds the blast radius and the ways to meet the goal before choosing to ask or draft.\\n- The launch allowance (saved calls or `--shape-budget CALLS`) defaults to zero; each step counts one before the model starts.\\n  With a current question and one run remaining, show `Drafting runs left this launch: 1 of M.`\\n  beside the answer editor before F2 spends it, using Think's shared budget wording.\\n  Budget policy stays behind Agent; Shape owns presentation (architecture diagnostics 3 and 6).\\n  Exhaustion refuses answer, defer, delegate, revision and teach-back before saving anything and explains how to allow calls.\\n- Tinkery, never the model, publishes answers and questions with the displayed version\\n  or the version at step start. Stale versions refuse, retain\\n  typed words and trigger a fresh read, never overwrite.\\n- Tinkery's bundled copy of the [seed contract source](https://github.com/jon-devlapaz/seed-me/blob/c9d766760dbeac0c05c92108165f9e968bec0a66/skills/seed-me/references/seed-contract.md)\\n  defines the artifact. Tinkery's ledger owns its canonical Full heading sequence;\\n  the reply fields and writer derive from that one layout. The model supplies\\n  `confirming` as an object: `You are confirming` contains exactly five non-empty\\n  summary lines, and each model-written prose section has its own string field named\\n  for the section, without heading syntax. Field order is immaterial. The summary\\n  covers goal, what gets built, what does not, the proposed first slice, and unknowns.\\n  Counts and reversal indicators belong to the ledger-computed confirmation summary.\\n  Drafting instructions retain names supplied\\n  in the confirmed goal or Think answers, including in the summary and knowledge\\n  map; a supplied tool name does not settle its executable path or invocation.\\n  Missing, blank, non-string or foreign fields\\n  refuse; prose cannot inject headings, fences, metadata or confirmation lines.\\n  Refusals name the rule and field, plus the offending line for structural text.\\n  A historical Markdown reply beginning `## You are confirming` is refused naming\\n  `confirming`, never with a generic format error.\\n  Shape attaches the bundled reference's section content guidance and check schema,\\n  not its instructions to write or paste artifact headings. The prompt defers to the\\n  generated field instructions, so there is no competing model-written layout.\\n  Tinkery writes every heading, `status: draft`, the goal-headline title,\\n  `revision: rN` one past the previous draft, and a separate `date:` line with the\\n  operator's local date (receipts stay UTC). An older writer can still increment the\\n  revision after rollback. Never replace a confirmed seed or draft with an open decision.\\n  Acceptance criteria, Decisions, Assumed and Evidence and uncertainty come only from\\n  recorded checks, decisions, assumptions and findings, in their canonical positions.\\n  Host-owned headings use LF; prose keeps its line endings. Ledger-owned blocks remain\\n  verbatim, with no extra wrappers. The exact generated title and origin-decision\\n  line treat goal comment markers as literal data during seed verification, only\\n  outside an existing comment. Their text and the confirmed goal remain unchanged;\\n  general heading and prose validation still refuse injected structure.\\n  Findings and question transport are unchanged.\\n- **Completion review runs within drafting**, with no extra call. Before producing a seed,\\n  the step compares settled decisions for contradictions and separates choices (`decided`)\\n  from observed completed work (`done`). Each model check carries its own non-empty\\n  `failure_case` string, including provisional and judge checks. The decoder removes this\\n  model-only field before canonical check validation and pairs it with that check's exact\\n  final statement; the model need not count a second list or copy statements (#469).\\n  A new blocker returns as a question, not a seed. The typed `review` object requires\\n  `contradictions`, `decided` and `done`. Older replies with ordered `review.failure_cases`\\n  strings still work strictly; mixed formats, missing cases and malformed cases refuse.\\n  Tinkery never duplicates, drops or invents cases to make coverage fit. Recorded clinic\\n  count mismatches and statement/case-object replies remain refusals.\\n  Saved check and review formats are unchanged. The ledger's `CompletionReview::validate`\\n\\n[Showing lines 1-716 of 1023 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=717 to continue.]\"}\n==> text 4/5 <==\n{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Prove thought protections by introducing three faults, then restore sources and binary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT/'tests'))\\nimport test_launch\\n\\nTHOUGHT = ROOT/'src/tend/thought.rs'\\nCONNECTION = ROOT/'src/tend/connection.rs'\\nFAULTS = [\\n    ('confirmed-goal', THOUGHT, '        let path = self.file(words)?;', '''        crate::seed_me::Config::new(Some(root.parent().unwrap().join(\\\"sessions\\\"))).confirm_as(\\n            crate::seed_me::Affirmed {\\n                goal: words.lines().next().unwrap().trim().into(), outcome: String::new(), options: vec![], originals: vec![],\\n                context: String::new(), source: \\\"TEST faulty thought confirmation\\\".into(),\\n            },\\n            &crate::think_record::GoalConfirmation::terminal(Some(\\\"agent\\\"))?,\\n        )?;\\n        let path = self.file(words)?;''', 'A thought changed goal sessions'),\\n    ('changed-words', THOUGHT, '            words: words.into(),',\\n     '            words: words.trim().into(),', 'Saved words differ from typed words'),\\n    ('provider-source', CONNECTION, '        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));', '''        for entry in fs::read_dir(&self.store).map_err(|e| e.to_string())? {\\n            let path = entry.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?.path();\\n            if path.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().starts_with(\\\"thought-\\\") {\\n                let thought: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(path).unwrap()).unwrap();\\n                if thought[\\\"repo\\\"] == serde_json::json!(self.repo) {\\n                    sources.push(Source { id: \\\"TEST-thought\\\".into(),\\n                        goal: thought[\\\"words\\\"].as_str().unwrap().into(), repo: self.repo.clone(),\\n                        status: \\\"active\\\".into() });\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        sources.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));''', 'A thought reached the provider request'),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    env = test_launch.environment()\\n    output = ROOT/'target/thought-probes'\\n    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    originals = {p: p.read_text() for p in [THOUGHT, CONNECTION]}\\n\\n    def build():\\n        test_launch.run(['cargo', '+stable', 'build', '--locked', '--quiet'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n    try:\\n        for name, path, old, new, expected in FAULTS:\\n            source = originals[path]\\n            if source.count(old) != 1:\\n                raise SystemExit(f'{name}: mutation no longer matches exactly once')\\n            path.write_text(source.replace(old, new))\\n            try:\\n                build()\\n                result = test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env,\\n                                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)\\n                log = result.stdout + result.stderr\\n                (output/f'{name}.log').write_text(log)\\n                if result.returncode == 0 or expected not in log:\\n                    raise SystemExit(f'{name}: protection did not fail for the expected reason\\\\n{log}')\\n                print(f'{name}: rejected ({expected})', flush=True)\\n            finally:\\n                path.write_text(source)\\n    finally:\\n        for path, source in originals.items():\\n            path.write_text(source)\\n        build()\\n    test_launch.run([sys.executable, 'tests/tend_thought_terminal.py'], cwd=ROOT, env=env, check=True)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    main()\\n\"}\n==> text 5/5 <==\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/\nruns/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/thought-journeys.log\nscripts/probe-thoughts.py\nsrc/tend/thought.rs\ntests/tend_thought_terminal.py\n\n[Full output: /var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt (read with offset/limit)]"}],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9109159999970871},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.9104169999991427},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/3","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":1.5290420000019367},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/4","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"scripts/probe-thoughts.py\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.5485420000004524},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/5","name":"find","args":"{\"pattern\":\"*thought*\"}","status":"ok","durationMs":11.119833999997354}],"fullOutputPath":"/var/folders/sk/r2ns7lvn2ygcsj7bhd0mvnyw0000gn/T/pi-codemode-fd4224656f9782a6.txt"},"isError":false,"durationMs":49,"timestamp":1794733047304,"nestedCalls":{"calls":[{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/1","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/REPAIR-BRIEF.md"},"durationMs":1},{"id":"call_65d275f619a848c38b101e4346379db1|ctc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af973f5882887d19b0e4de827ec88fe/2","name":"read","status":"ok","arguments":{"path":"runs/issue-864-tend-thought/03-build/output/handoff.md"},"durationMs":1},{