{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_0a2bcc2e70584d4fa0a72cb4a7fa7159|fc_0cb7c24900cb2122016af9751d57ac87d1aa4656339971d048","toolName":"edit","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md."}],"details":{"diff":"      ...\n   27 \n   28 In this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\n   29 the repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\n   30 call and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\n+  31 The summary shows `t new thought`, even before any thought is saved, and `v read`\n+  32 when thoughts exist. These keys leave the goal garden's key bar unchanged.\n   31 `v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\n   32 `g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\n   33 Think goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\n   34 Thoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\n      ...\n   38 and exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\n   39 Identical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\n   40 Whitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\n   41 empty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\n-  42 never edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\n+  44 never edited or replaced. A malformed or unsupported thought does not hide readable thoughts.\n+  45 The garden and reader show how many thoughts could not be read. Store failures remain visible\n+  46 instead of becoming an empty list.\n   43 \n   44 Inside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\n   45 origin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\n   46 `a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\n      ...","patch":"--- docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\n+++ docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\n@@ -27,8 +27,10 @@\n \n In this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\n the repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\n call and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\n+The summary shows `t new thought`, even before any thought is saved, and `v read`\n+when thoughts exist. These keys leave the goal garden's key bar unchanged.\n `v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\n `g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\n Think goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\n Thoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\n@@ -38,9 +40,11 @@\n and exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\n Identical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\n Whitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\n empty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\n-never edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\n+never edited or replaced. A malformed or unsupported thought does not hide readable thoughts.\n+The garden and reader show how many thoughts could not be read. Store failures remain visible\n+instead of becoming an empty list.\n \n Inside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\n origin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\n `a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\n","firstChangedLine":31}},"isError":false,"durationMs":3}
